\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The rate differential between bonds with Argentine and foreign law is the highest since debt exchange\b0\par\par\uc2 963 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Despite the recent improvement, the spread by legislation recently reached its highest level since debt exchange, amid indefinitions over an agreement with the Paris Club and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Recent news of negotiations with agencies positively affected bonds, although the impact was greater on foreign law.\par \par \uc2 At times of increased uncertainty regarding the ability to pay Argentina's debt commitments, investors tend to favor foreign-underned securities, to the detriment of local law.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks we have seen a steady expansion in spreads of local law bonds over those of foreign legislation. That is, those governed by Argentine law show higher yields than those that respond to international laws, which is justified on the basis that the latter show greater relative demand.\par \par \uc2 In this way, the spread by legislation averages 165 basis points, and in some tranches, the spread reaches the highest level since debt exchange.\par \par \uc2 The spread between laws in the short tranche (bonds at 2029 and 2030) operates with a rate differential of approximately 165 points. This implies a record since restructuring for bonds by 2030 while by 2029 it means trading in the highs zone since debt redemption.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, those who expire in 2035 trade a spread of 50 basic points, which is also at a higher rank since debt exchange.\par \par \uc2 Finally, in the longer sections, at 2038 and 2041, high differential levels are also observed and in areas of maximums since redemption.\par \par \uc2 Pedro Siaba Serrate, a strata of Portfolio Personal Inversiones (PPI), added that from late March until now, the weighted average price of securities bounced from the post-restructuring lows to levels he did not see since mid-February, with greater focus in recent days thanks to the good climate of global emerging debt and positive signs regarding renegotiation with the Paris Club.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, he added that there was particularity that NY Law instruments received this rebound more directly while local titles lagged behind.\par \par \uc2 "Looking at the historical evolution, the weighted spread legislation peaked at 169 base points during the holiday Tuesday, although on Wednesday with activity in the local square, this spread was rearranged in the area of 151 basic points," said PPI's strata.\par \par \uc2 With a similar view, Julio Calcagnino, market analyst at TSA Stock Market Group of the Transatlantic Group, stressed that until last week, all Argentine dollar bonds traded with a above-average legislation gap observed throughout 2021 for each case.\par \par \uc2 "At the cross-sectional level, the largest spread was observed in 2029 and 2038, both above the average of all papers. In May, foreign law bonds were revalued more than their local counterparts. Without a clear impact of Fernandez and Guzman's tour in Europe on debt negotiation processes with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and the Paris Club, all of this would point to opportunity purchases due to widespread devaluation of local roles," Calcagnino said.\par \par \uc2 The TSA Stock Market specialist also recalled that some foreign investment banks, such as Citi, recommended the construction of long positions on Argentine bonds, mainly GD29 and GD30, in view of a possible pro-opposition election scenario.\par \par \uc2 "The spread movement could be due to some timely appetite from outside investors, who would opt for international law bonds to the detriment of local ones," he said.\par \par \uc2 Causes of spread expansion\par \par \uc2 Spread expansion is generally associated with increased uncertainty regarding Argentina's ability to re-pay its debt, so investors seek protection on assets with legal jurisdiction abroad to the detriment of bonds governed by local courts.\par \par \uc2 However, market analysts add other issues related to flows and dollarization of portfolios to explain this behavior.\par \par \uc2 Rodrigo Ben\u237\'00\'EDtez, chief economist of Quinquela Fondos, explained that the spread of legislation has been expanding to the extent that the value of bonds falls and they are operated with parities in mind, i.e. their recovery value in the event of non-payment.\par \par \uc2 In other words, when bonds fall, the risks associated with a credit event tend to grow and investors are often looking for greater protection in foreign-underned bonds at that time.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the chief economist of Quinquela Fondos argued that the spread between legislation currently shows heterogeneous situations depending on the term of the bonds and is explained by issues of dollarization of portfolios.\par \par \uc2 "In the short sections (2029-2030) the spread is higher and is in line with the maximum levels since its issuance (7.7% in 2029 and 9.3% in 2030). This situation may be explained in the volume of portfolio dollarization \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These bonds, for their higher liquidity, are the most commonly used for The Settlement Count (CCL) and MEP transactions. In addition, they are the ones used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in these markets containing spreads. That is to say that they are the bonds that have the highest demand both in their \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in pesos and in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the economist said.\par \par \uc2 Finally, Benitez noted that investors betting on long-term holdings choose foreign law, on the other hand those who only use them as instruments to dollarize operate preferably under local law.\par \par \uc2 In this line, he said that two particularities have been combined over the past week that have impacted the spread by legislation: "First, the political uncertainty that has been generated around the official position in view of the outstanding negotiations with the Paris Club and the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ," he explained\par \par \uc2 "On the other hand, while there were maturities of peso bonds of more than $60 billion held by foreign investors, the bulk of portfolio dollarization \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain local traders, who use bonds under Argentine law to dollarize, but immediately sell those positions," he said.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210528eh5s0081s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw109\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1635\pichgoal600
