g foreign trade loans and U.S. dollars loans totaled Ps.92.4 billion in 2020, representing a 12.3% decrease from Ps.105.4 billion in 2019. The decrease in the average balance of our total loan portfolio (excluding foreign trade loans and U.S. dollar loans) is mainly explained by the following changes in average balance portfolio: (i) 32.0% or Ps.10.0 billion decrease in personal loans, (ii) 30.4% or Ps.2.9 billion decrease in overdraft, and (iii) 39.0% or Ps.2.4 billion decrease in receivable from financial leases. These were partially offset by 18.3% or Ps. 2.7 billion increase in corporate unsecured loans and 16.7% or Ps. 2.1 billion increase in promissory notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest on public and corporate securities measured at amortized cost amounted to Ps.20.5 billion in 2020. This line item mainly reflects results from investments in securities held to maturity or available for sale.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The average interest rate on total loans (excluding foreign trade loans and U.S. dollar loans) decreased to 41.5% in 2020 from 51.8% in 2019. Average BADLAR decreased 1,970 basis points in 2020 to 29.7% compared to 48.7% in 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ii) Interest Expenses\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Our Interest expenses were comprised of the following:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                               As of December 31,                  Change December 31,   \par                                                               2020                                2019                                 2020/2019 \par                                                                                    Ps.                                    Ps.                %       \par Interest on special checking accounts                                              6,325,123                              8,182,612          (22.7   %) \par Interest on time deposits                                                          19,574,998       