 authorized by the CNV through Resolution No. 19,958 dated December 27, 2018. The Bank is registered with the CNV as a frequent issuer of Negotiable Obligations under No. 03. At the board meeting of the company on March 7, 2019, it was resolved to approve the Bank's ratification in the Frequent Issuer Regime and at the Board meeting on December 2, 2019 it was resolved to allocate the maximum amount of U.S.$300,000,000 corresponding to the Global Issuance Program of Negotiable Obligations for up to U.S.$2,300,000,000, with the bank in the process of reducing the maximum amount of said Program. The CNV approved said ratification through Resolution DI-2020-11-APN-GE #CNV dated February 11, 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On June 12, 2020, the Board of Directors of Banco Supervielle SA, approved the issuance of its Class G Non-Subordinated Negotiable Obligation for an amount that will not exceed in its N/V U.S.$30,000,000 set within the Global Program of Negotiable Obligations. It was also approved to modify the terms of said issuance, so that the Issue Amount is up to U.S.$50,000,000 and without prejudice to the fact that the Negotiable Obligations are denominated in U.S. dollars, they may be integrated and payments under them can be made in pesos. The bidding period ended on June 25, 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2020, and 2019, the amounts outstanding and the terms corresponding to outstanding unsubordinated negotiable obligations were as follows (with figures expressed in thousands of Pesos):\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Class                         Issue Date     Maturity Date     Annual Interest Rate      12/31/2020                 12/31/2019   \par Banco Supervielle Class A     02/09/2017     08/09/2020        Badlar + Spread 4.5%                   -                            5,179,248   \par Banco Supervielle Class C     12/22/2017     12/22/2021        Badlar + Spread 4.25%                  444,327                      908,288     \par Banco Supervie