garding the transferred portfolio, and therefore, such portfolio meets derecognition requirements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 9. REPO AND REVERSE REPO TRANSACTIONS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group carries out repo transactions in which it performs the spot sale of a security with the related forward purchase thereof, thus substantially retaining all the risks and rewards associated with the instruments and recognizing them in 'Repo Transactions' at year-end, as the provisions set out in point 3.4.2 (Derecognition of Assets) of IFRS 9 'Financial Instruments') are not met.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The residual values \u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0Bof assets transferred under repo and reverse repo transactions as of December 31, 2020 and 2019 are detailed below:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Repo Transactions:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                       Book Value   \par December 31, 2020     -            \par December 31, 2019     435,401      \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reverse Repo Transactions:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                       Book Value   \par December 31, 2020     22,354,735   \par December 31, 2019     -            \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-55\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GRUPO SUPERVIELLE S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2020, presented in comparative format\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Expressed in thousands of pesos)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10. DERIVATIVE FINANCIAL INSTRUMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the normal course of business, the Group enters into a variety of transactions principally in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stock markets. Most counterparties in the derivative transactions are banks and other financial institutions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 These instruments include:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Forwards and futures: they are agreements to deliver or take delivery at a specified rate, price or index applied against the underlying asset or financial instrument, at a specific date. Futures are exchange traded at standardized amounts of the underlying asset or financial instrument.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Forwards contracts are OTC agreements and are principally dealt in by the Group in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as forward agreements.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Swaps: they are agreements between two parties with the intention to exchange cash flows and risks at specific date and for a period in the future. - Options: they confer the right to the buyer, but no obligation, to receive or pay a specific quantity of an asset or financial instrument for a specified price at or before a specified date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2020 and 2019, the following amounts were recorded for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  related to derivatives:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                             12/31/2020               12/31/2019   \par Amounts receivable for spot and forward transactions pending settlement                  143,944                    350,680   \par Amounts payable for spot and forward transactions pending settlement                     -                          -         \par                                                                                          143,944                    350,680   \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table shows, the notional value of options and outstanding forward and futures contracts as of December 31, 2020 and 2019:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                 12/31/2020                 12/31/2019   \par Forward sales of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  without delivery of underlying assets                      3,189,269                    446,195   \par Forward purchases of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  without delivery of underlying assets                  1,647,980                    579,188   \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The incomes/(expenses) generated by derivative financial instruments during the years ended December 31, 2020 and 2019 amounted to 180,102 and 971,521 respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 11. EARNINGS PER SHARE\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earnings per share are calculated by dividing income attributable to the Group\u180\'00\'B4s shareholders by the weighted average number of outstanding common shares during the period. As the Group does not have preferred shares or debt convertible into shares, basic earnings are equal to diluted earnings per share.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                      12/31/2020                 12/31/2019                  12/31/2018   \par Income attributable to shareholders of the group                  3,499,882                    (2,929,201   )                (6,341,497   ) \par Weighted average of ordinary shares (thousands)                   456,722                      456,722                       456,722      \par Income per share                                                  7.66                         (6.41        )                (13.88       ) \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-56\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GRUPO SUPERVIELLE S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Notes to Consolidated Financial Statements\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2020, presented in comparative format\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Expressed in thousands of pesos)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12. SPECIAL TERMINATION ARRANGEMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Special termination arrangements are principally termination benefits payable to employees who accepted a pre-retirement offer. These benefits are payable during the period between their effective termination date and their retirement age, when they voluntarily accept an irrevocable termination arrangement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of Dec