o environmental, health and safety matters \u183\'00\'B7 Limitations on local pricing in Argentina may adversely affect our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results \u183\'00\'B7 Our activities may be adversely affected by events in other countries in which we do business\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks Relating to our Shares and ADSs\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 Restrictions on the movement of capital out of Argentina may impair the ability of holders of ADSs to receive dividends and distributions, and the proceeds of any sale of, the shares underlying the ADSs, which could affect the market value of the ADSs \u183\'00\'B7 ADS holders' ability to receive cash dividends may be limited \u183\'00\'B7 Under Argentine law, shareholder rights may be fewer or less well-defined than in other jurisdictions \u183\'00\'B7 Holders of ADSs may be unable to exercise voting rights with respect to the common shares underlying the ADSs at our shareholders' meetings \u183\'00\'B7 Our shareholders may be subject to liability for certain votes of their securities \u183\'00\'B7 Provisions of our bylaws and of Argentine securities laws could deter takeover attempts and have an adverse impact on the price of our shares and the ADSs\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 9\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \u183\'00\'B7 There can be no assurance that we will not be a passive foreign investment company, or PFIC, for U.S. federal income tax purposes for any taxable year, which could subject U.S. holders of our shares or ADSs to adverse U.S. federal income tax consequences.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risks Related to Argentina\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Overview\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We are a stock corporation (sociedad an\u243\'00\'F3nima) incorporated under the laws of the Republic of Argentina and most of our revenues are earned in Argentina and most of our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , facilities and customers are located in Argentina. Our financial condition and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results depend to a significant extent on macroeconomic, regulatory, political and financial conditions prevailing in Argentina, including growth rates, inflation rates, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, taxes, interest rates, and other local, regional and international events and conditions that may affect Argentina in any manner. For example, a slowdown in economic growth or economic recession could lead to a decreased demand for electricity in the service areas in which we and our subsidiaries operate or a decline in the purchasing power of our customers, which, in turn, could lead to a higher delinquency rate from our customers or increased energy losses due to illegal use of our services. Actions of the Argentine Government concerning the economy, including measures with respect to inflation, interest rates, price controls (including tariffs and other compensation of utility companies), \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls and taxes, have had and may in the future have a material adverse effect on private sector entities, including us. Our activities are highly regulated and subject to uncertainties due to political and economic factors, changes in legislation, expropriations, termination and modification of contractual rights, revocation of permits and consents, the need to obtain permits from regulatory authorities, foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  restrictions, price controls, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fluctuations and increases in royalties, among others.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 We cannot assure you that the Argentine Government will not adopt policies that could adversely affect the Argentine economy or our business, financial condition or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results. In addition, we cannot assure you that future economic, regulatory, social and political developments in Argentina will not impair our business, financial condition or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results, or cause the market value of our ADSs and common shares to decline.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A global or regional financial crisis and unfavorable credit and market conditions may negatively affect our liquidity, customers, business and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The effects of a global or regional financial crisis and related turmoil in the global financial system may have a negative impact on our business, capacity to access credit and international capital markets, financial condition and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  results, which is likely to be more severe on an emerging market economy, such as Argentina (See '-Argentina's ability to obtain financing from international markets could be limited, which may impair its ability to implement reforms and foster economic growth and, consequently, affect our business, results of our \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and growth prospects.' below). This was the case in 2008, when the global economic crisis led to a sudden economic decline in Argentina in 2009, accompanied by inflationary pressures, depreciation of the Peso and a drop in consumer and investor confidence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The effects of an economic crisis on our customers and on us cannot be predicted. Weak global and local economic conditions could lead to reduced demand or lower prices for energy, hydrocarbons and related oil products and petrochemicals, which could have a negative effect on our revenues. Economic factors such as unemployment, inflation and the unavailability of credit could also have a material adverse effect on the demand for