enerating return for its shareholders and benefits to other stakeholders, and keeping an optimal capital structure to reduce the cost of capital.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To keep or adjust its capital structure, the Company may adjust the amount of the dividends paid to its shareholders, reimburse capital to its shareholders, issue new shares, conduct stock repurchase programs or sell assets to reduce its debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In line with industry practices, the Company monitors its capital based on the leverage ratio. This ratio is calculated by dividing the net debt by the total capital. The net debt equals the total indebtedness (including current and non-current indebtedness) minus cash and cash equivalents and current financial assets at fair value through profit and loss. The total capital corresponds to the shareholders' equity as shown in the statement of financial position, plus the net debt.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Financial leverage ratios as at December 31, 2020 and 2019 were as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                                 12.31.2020     12.31.2019 \par Total borrowings                                                                                1,614          1,947 \par Less: cash and cash equivalents, and financial assets at fair value through profit and loss     (466)          (590) \par Net debt                                                                                        1,148          1,357 \par Total capital attributable to owners                                                            2,576          3,274 \par Leverage ratio                                                                                  44.57%         41.45% \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-106\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTES TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018 (Continuation)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (in millions of US$ - unless otherwise stated)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTE 7: SEGMENT INFORMATION\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company is a fully integrated power company in Argentina, which participates in the electricity and oil and gas value chains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Through its own activities, subsidiaries and share holdings in joint ventures, and based on the business nature, customer portfolio and risks involved, we were able to identify the following business segments:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electricity Generation, principally consisting of the Company's direct and indirect interests in HINISA, HIDISA, Greenwind, CTB, TMB, TJSM and through its own electricity generation activities through thermal plants G\u252\'00\'FCemes, Piedra Buena, Piquirenda, Loma de la Lata, Genelba and Ecoenerg\u237\'00\'EDa, Pilar, I. White, the Pichi Pic\u250\'00\'FAn Leuf\u250\'00\'FA hydroelectric complex and Pampa Energ\u237\'00\'EDa I and II wind farms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electricity Distribution, consisting of the Company's direct interest in Edenor. As of December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018, the Company has classified the results corresponding to the divestment mentioned in Note 5.3.1 as discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , for each of the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil and Gas, consisting of the Company's own interests in oil and gas areas and through its direct interest in PACOSA and indirectly interest in OCP. As of December 31, 2018 the Company has classified the results corresponding to the divestment mentioned in Note 5.3.2 as discontinued \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Petrochemicals, comprising of the Company's own styrenics \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the catalytic reformer plant \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  conducted in Argentine plants.\f28