            (911) \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-146\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTES TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018 (Continuation)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (in millions of US$ - unless otherwise stated)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTE 12: (Continuation)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 12.8 Fair value of financial Instruments\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Company classifies the fair value measurements of financial instruments using a fair value hierarchy, which reflects the relevance of the variables used to perform those measurements. The fair value hierarchy has the following levels:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Level 1: quoted prices (not adjusted) for identical assets or liabilities in active markets. - Level 2: data different from the quoted prices included in Level 1 observable for the asset or liability, either directly (i.e. prices) or indirectly (i.e. derived from prices). - Level 3: Asset or liability data based on information that cannot be observed in the market (i.e., unobservable data).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following table shows the Company's financial assets and liabilities measured at fair value as of December 31, 2020 and 2019:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2020                                    Level 1     Level 2     Level 3     Total \par Assets                                                                                         \par Financial assets at fair value throughprofit and losss                                         \par Government securities                                      204         -           -           204 \par Shares                                                     29          -           11          40 \par Investment funds                                           92          -           -           92 \par Cash and cash equivalents                                                                      \par Investment funds                