Ps.1.7 billion from Ps.1.9 billion in 2019\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net Financial Income (Net Interest Income (NII), Net Income from Financial Instruments (NIFFI) and Exchange Rate Differences on Gold and Foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net Financial Income\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net financial income in 2020 amounted to Ps.41.2 billion and net interest margin (NIM) was 21.5%, compared to Ps.41.5 billion, and 21.0%, respectively, in 2019.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NIM in 2020 reflects (i) a higher proportion of average Peso Interest Earning Assets on total average Interest Earning Assets. NIM in Ps. decreased to 22.6% form 28.2% mainly due to higher proportion of average balance of Ps. investment portfolio on total average Peso Interest Earning Assets compared to 2019 reflecting higher average holdings in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LELIQs and Repo transactions to take advantage of higher spreads as average cost of funds decreased 1,500 bps. Loan portfolio NIM in Pesos increased by 170 bps to 25.9% from 24.2% mainly due to the decrease in cost of fund, partially offset by weak credit demand, higher credit cards volumes related to government sponsored programs, 'Ahora 12' and 'Previaje,' iii) lower yields on loans following the decrease in market interest rates and also due to credit lies granted to SMEs at preferential interest rates. Since April 2020, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ruled a minimum floor on interest rates paid on time deposits reducing the deceleration of the Cost of Funds along the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Breakdown Net Interest Income, NIFFI, Result from derecognition of assets measured at amortized cost and Exchange Rate Differences\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                                                                                                        Grupo Supervielle S.A.   \par               