al Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Those deposits acquired through endorsement and those deposits made as a result of incentives other than interest rate are also excluded. This system has been implemented through the creation of the Deposit Insurance Fund ('FGD'), which is managed by a company called Seguros de Dep\u243\'00\'F3sitos S.A. ('SEDESA'). The shareholders of SEDESA are the Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the financial institutions, in the proportion determined for each one by the Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  based on the contributions made to the fund.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 22. RESTRICTED ASSETS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As of December 31, 2020 and 2019, the following Grupo Supervielle's assets are restricted:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Item                                                         12/31/2020                 12/31/2019   \par Financial assets in guarantee                                                                                      \par Special guarantee accounts in the Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                   3,710,757                    2,887,162   \par Trust guarantee deposits                                                  -                            5,173       \par Guarantee deposits for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forward transactions                      601,248                      2,865,356   \par Guarantee deposits for credit cards transactions                          421,942                      432,118     \par Other guarantee deposits                                                  160,820                      215,866     \par Guarantee deposits for repo transactions                                  -                            32,510      \par                                                                           4,894,76