 the effects of the individual exemptions granted by the Superintendence of Financial and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Institutions) or minimum cash, v) they shall have complied with additional capital margin when applicable.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The entities not facing any of these situations may distribute dividends in accordance with provisions set forth in said amended text, provided the entity\u180\'00\'B4s liquidity or solvency is not jeopardized.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is worth to be mentioned that pursuant to Communication 'A' 6464 issued by the Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , until March 31, 2020, financial entities, which, for the purpose of determining the distributable result, have not applied the additional on capital margins shall rely on previous authorization issued by the SEFyC.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On August 30, 2019 and with the purpose of stabilizing the exchange market, the Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issued Communication 'A' 6768, pursuant which financial entities shall rely on the previous authorization of Exchange and Financial Entities Superintendence before distributing its income. Over the course of such authorization process, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will assess, among other items, potential effects of the application of international accounting standards pursuant to Communication 'A' 6430 (Paragraph 5.5 of IFRS 9 - Detriment of financial assets value) as well as the effects of the re-expression of financial statements pursuant to Communication 'A' 6651.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On March 19, 2020 the Argentine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issued Communication 'A' 6939 by means of which the suspension of income distribution of financial entities was made effective until June 30, 2020.\f28 \par \par \uc2