 primarily the result of:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a Ps.318.62 million, or 59.35%, increase in taxes on bank account transactions as a result of the revenue increase during the year ended December 31, 2019; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a Ps. 292.15 million, or 40.68%, increase in fees and compensation for services.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2020 Compared to 2019\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In 2020, we recorded a Ps. 4.02 billion impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets charge, mainly related to a reduction in the assessed value-in-use of certain assets that exceeded their previously recorded book value, mainly related to our Brigadier L\u243\'00\'F3pez plant and intangible assets associated to it, our Lujan de Cuyo Combined Cycle plant and some of the gas turbines that the company holds for potential new projects. Some of the factors that influenced this reduction were the limited useful life of these assets, the drop in the Company's stock price, the current economic uncertainties, the suspension of the spot market price update mechanism established by Resolution 31, and in the particular case of the Company's gas turbines, the uncertainty about the feasibility of new projects that would enable the use of the acquired turbines. For further information, see 'Item 5.A. Operating Results - Critical Accounting Policies - Impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets.'\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In 2019, we recorded a Ps. 6.00 billion impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets charge, mainly related to a reduction in the assessed value-in-use of certain assets that exceeded their previously recorded book value, mainly related to our Brigadier L\u243\'00\'F3pez plant and intangible assets associated to it and some of the gas turbines that the company holds for potential new projects. Some of the factors that influenced this reduction were the limited useful life of these assets, the drop in the Company\u180\'00\'B4s stock price, the current economic uncertainties, the conversion of the electric and power spot market tariff into Argentine pesos, and in the particular case of the Company's gas turbines, the uncertainty about the feasibility of new projects that would enable the use of the acquired turbines. For further information, see 'Item 5.A. Operating Results - Critical Accounting Policies - Impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets.'\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2019 Compared to 2018\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In 2019, we recorded a Ps. 6.00 billion impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets charge, mainly related to a reduction in the assessed value-in-use of certain assets that exceeded their previously recorded book value, mainly related to our Brigadier L\u243\'00\'F3pez plant and intangible assets associated to it and some of the gas turbines that the company holds for potential new projects. Some of the factors that influenced this reduction were the limited useful life of these assets, the drop in the Company\u180\'00\'B4s stock price, the current economic uncertainties, the conversion of the electric and power spot market tariff into Argentine pesos, and in the particular case of the Company's gas turbines, the uncertainty about the feasibility of new projects that would enable the use of the acquired turbines. For further information, see Item 5.A. Operating Results - Critical Accounting Policies - Impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In 2018, we did not record any Impairment of property, plant and equipment and intangible assets charge.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Operating Income from continuing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 2020 Compared to 2019\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Other operating income 