                                                2,623,754                                                                     16,523,244\par Amortization for the year 690,229          66,977                                                     1,577,093                                                                     2,334,299\par Impairment                -                -                                                          599,204                                                                       599,204\par 12-31-2020                14,484,095       172,601                                                    4,800,051                                                                     19,456,747\par                           \par \par Net book value\par                           \par \par 12-31-2019                2,760,916        1,189,406                                                  5,673,166                                                                     9,623,488\par 12-31-2020                2,070,687        1,176,550                                                  3,496,869                                                                     6,744,106\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (1)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transferred from property, plant and equipment. See below.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concession right of Piedra del \u193\'00\'C1guila hydroelectric power plant\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Includes the amounts paid as consideration for rights relating to the concession of Piedra del \u193\'00\'C1guila hydroelectric power plant awarded by the Argentine government for a 30-year term, until December 29, 2023. The Group amortizes such intangible asset based on straight-line basis over the remaining life of the concession agreement.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For a concession arrangement to fall within the scope of IFRIC 12, usage of the infrastructure must be controlled by the concession grantor. This requirement is met when the following two conditions are met:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the grantor controls or regulates what services the operator must provide with the infrastructure, to whom it must provide them, and at what price; and\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the grantor controls the infrastructure, i.e., retains the right to take back the infrastructure at the end of the concession.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Upon Resolution 95 passed by Argentine government the Company\u180\'00\'B4s concession right of Piedra del \u193\'00\'C1guila hydroelectric power plant met both conditions above.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The main features of the concession contract are as follows:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Control and regulation of prices by concession grantor: Pricing schedule approved by grantor;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Remuneration paid by: CAMMESA;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Grant or guarantee from concession grantor: None;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 F-48\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CENTRAL PUERTO S.A.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Residual value: Infrastructure returned to grantor for no consideration at end of concession;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concession end date: December 29, 2023;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IFRIC 12 accounting model: Intangible asset.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fees and royalties: the Intergovernmental Basin Authority is entitled to a fee of 2.5% of the plant's revenues, and the provinces of Rio Negro and Neuqu\u233\'00\'E9n are entitled to royalties of 12% of such revenues. For the years ended December 31, 2020, 2019 and 2018, the fees and royalties amounted 367,787, 329,714 and 312,291, respectively and they were shown in operating expenses in the consolidated statement of income.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Contractual capital investment obligations and obligations relating to maintenance expenditure on infrastructure under concession are not significant.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transmission lines of wind farms Achiras and La Castellana\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group finished the construction of wind farms La Castellana and Achiras, whereby the Group agreed to build high and medium tension lines and the electrical substation to connect the wind farms to SADI, a part of which were given to the companies transporting the energy in accordance with the respective contracts; therefore, such companies are in charge of the maintenance of such transferred installations. Consequently, the Group recognized intangible assets for the works related to the construction of the described equipments.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electrical substation of wind farm La Genoveva II\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During 2019 the Group finished the construction of wind farm La Genoveva II, whereby the Group agreed to build the electrical substation that feeds the connection of the wind farm to the SADI, a part of which were given to the company transporting the energy; therefore, such company is in charge of the maintenance of such transferred installations. Consequently, the Group recognized intangible assets for an amount of 33,722, which were transferred from property, plant and equipment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Electrical substation of wind farm La Genoveva\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During 2020 the Group finished the construction of wind farm La Genoveva, whereby the Group agreed to build the electrical substation that feeds the connection of the wind farm to the SADI, a part of which were given to the company transporting the energy; therefore, such company is in charge of the maintenance of such transferred installations. Consequently, the Group recognized intangible assets for an amount of 50,122, which were transferred from property, plant and equipment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turbogas and turbosteam supply agreements for Thermal Station Brigadier L\u243\'00\'F3pez\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During fiscal year 2019, as a result of the business combination described in Note 2.2.20, the Group recognized an intangible asset for 8,296,920 related to turbogas and turbosteam supply agreements e