\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The collapse of Bitcoin, which began to recover last night, revealed a highly speculative market in Argentina\b0\par\par\uc2 828 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 April 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Local markets will be influenced by the behavior of Bitcoin that had a global collapse of more than 16% on Saturday, when it came to touch a $51,300 flat after it closed at $61,000 on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The problem was a blackout in China, in Xinjiang Province, where the world's largest Bitcoin miners are. Miners control issuance and transactions. There are scheduled 21 million Bitcoins issued for 2140 and miners are part of that control.\par \par \uc2 When the blackout occurred, vendors appeared fearing that the system could be hacked by this situation. The sale unleashed an unstoppable domino effect because many were played in the future and bought with leverage, i.e. with money that is not their own. Others made synthetic dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a combination of Bitcoin purchases or sales with dollar futures.\par \par \uc2 Computers, as the price fell, automatically closed the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of leveragers who run out of margin by accelerating the collapse. In addition, someone spread the rumor that the Fed was going to control and fine American banks for money laundering with cryptocurrencies and the \uc2 Twitter\uc2  social network was a hotbed of desperate investors looking for information from their peers. The curfew kept a lot of people awake on Saturday night. The cryptocurrency operates 24 hours a day without holidays.\par \par \uc2 When Bitcoin touched $51,000, buyers appeared that started raising the price and took the floor to $55,000. From there the fall stopped and a slow recovery began. A curious fact is that most transactions go through the miners of Paraguay where the cost of energy is cheaper. Bitcoin's annual transactions consume the energy of two Argentinas in one year. That's why the price of electricity is key for miners.\par \par \uc2 Cutting losses\par \par \uc2 At midnight on Sunday Bitcoin cut its losses to just over 6% and its price was slightly above USD 56 thousand. By Wednesday, he had reached a record $64,300. Ethereum, the other most traded cryptocurrency, lost 3.51% and traded at USD 2,237.2. But we will have to see how Bitcoin affects companies that accept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of payment and how it affects the exchanges, which in the overnite market were trading on negative ground. As we know, these trades start at 19.30 Argentine time and are bets on how the market will open on Monday. All three \uc2 New York Stock Exchange\uc2  indices were on negative ground with losses of 0.30%. In Europe, Madrid was neutral and Frankfurt down 0.31%. London fell 0.21% but the Eurostoxx 50, which takes the average of half a hundred of the most traded shares in the euro area, was up 1.16%.\par \par \uc2 The dollar in turn rose 0.08% against the world's six largest \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Bond rate was 1.57%, which is tolerable for the region's economies as they do not tempt capital to run away. In this sense, Brazil is a sign of strength because the San Pablo Stock Exchange threaded 5 consecutive hikes and the real one stands firm against the dollar without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And by house...\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar is accumulating tensions. This is demonstrated by the failure of the latest tenders where foreign funds, despite the advantageous rate of 2.20% on inflation given by the BONCER, chose to collect them and not accept the exchange even though that surcharge is higher than that of the rest of the Boncer issued. In other words, for Templeton and PIMCO the carry-trade is over (playing in pesos, taking the winnings and moving to dollars). These two funds are a risk to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's debt tenders until the end of May because they have in their portfolio bonds that expire in that period for the equivalent of USD 580 million that they do not plan to redeem, but will collect them in cash to transform them into dollars and through liquidation, taking them out of the country. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to lose reserves - and there will be few - if it wants to keep the price of alternative dollars in balance.\par \par \uc2 That is why this week, the tension on the dollar will continue and we will have to see how Argentina affects the fall in Bitcoin, although it is signaling recovery. This is a new market that is expanding in Argentina and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to regulate because it is not limited to the purchase and sale of the cryptocurrency, but that future and synthetic dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are made.\par \par \uc2 READ ON:\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and cryptocurrencies: 13 questions and answers about the phenomenon, on a day that once again showed the high volatility of digital assets\par \par \uc2 At the age of 83, the founder of \uc2 Adobe\uc2 , creator of programs such as PDF, Photoshop, Acrobat and Illustrator, died\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210419eh4j004zn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
