\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The lawfare against \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2 , seen from Brazil\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2  is one of the bravest leaders to have had Argentina and Latin America. He was - and continues to be - the victim of one of the most cowardly and absurd versions of lawfare.\par \par \uc2 His defense is an extraordinary piece, because he unmasks the charges against him, transforming them into charges against the Argentine judiciary and concluding that: "With this Justice there can be no democracy".\par \par \uc2 This absurd process - one of many he suffers - is about a policy of his government's future dollar, when he had as economy minister the current governor of the province of Buenos Aires, Axel Kiciloff. A policy that aimed to free Argentina from one of the chains that most hinders the advancement of the country's economy, because it is linked to the dollarization inherited from the 2001/2002 crisis.\par \par \uc2 You were both charged? to generate benefits for them and for friends and government officials, who would have been greatly enriched by that policy. A complaint made at the start of the race by the 2015 presidential election to favor \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 , a right-wing candidate, openly supported by the judiciary.\par \par \uc2 The then opponents, not content with the scandal they made in the complacent media, promoted actions in Cristina's house and at the headquarters of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the midst of the election campaign. Actions that had a decisive weight in the first round, which ended with Cristina's candidate, Daniel Scioli, with little advantage over Macri, facing the second round.\par \par \uc2 The accusations that have been prolonged over time have not prevented Cristina from being elected as a senator first and as vice president afterwards or kiciloff being elected governor of the province of Buenos Aires. But they reinforced the clich\u233\'00\'E9s in the media that peronists are corrupt, that Cristina is corrupt, clich\u233\'00\'E9s assumed even by some sectors of the left.\par \par \uc2 Well. Macri won the election and, contrary to what he had promised in the election campaign, made a large devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which Cristina was always accused of, but never did, because of the awareness of how hard this financial mechanism hits over the popular sectors of the country.\par \par \uc2 Time passed and, to general amazement, in an expertise of the judiciary, it was concluded that neither Cristina, nor Kiciloff, nor any friend or official of Cristina's government, had bought dollars and benefited from the policy of the future dollar. That conclusion was made public in 2020, five years after the war against Cristina and Macri's victory, which, as president, promoted a devaluation, used fundamental government advisers to profit - exactly what Cristina had been accused of - in the face of the silence and benevolence of Argentine judiciary and great media.\par \par \uc2 Cristina continues to answer for this absurd process. He made a spectacular and courageous oral defense, in which he reverses all the accusations and places on the judiciary serious responsibilities of political \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which led \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  to suffer four years of setback and new indebtedness to the \uc2 IMF\uc2  by \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This is one of the lawfare processes in Argentina, which fall to Cristina, similar to the equally unfounded processes that led Lula to jail and prevented him from being elected as Brazil's new president on the first lap, in 2018, which led the country to suffer the worst crisis in its history, with thousands of deaths daily , delayed vaccination, economic depression and social misery.\par \par \uc2 The same processes, which also fall to \uc2 Evo Morales\uc2  and Rafael Correa, preventing them from running for the presidency of their countries, but unable to prevent their supporting candidates from succeeding and undoing allgovernments that restored neoliberalism in Bolivia and Ecuador.\par \par \uc2 Cristina makes an undisputed defense of her behavior, destroys the arguments of the trials against her and accuses the Argentine judiciary of, through lawfare, judicialization of politics and anti-democratic interference in Argentine politics. In conclusion, in accordance with the thesis mentioned above and also defended by President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 , without the democratization of the judiciary, Argentina will never have a full democracy.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210313eh3c000ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
