\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The growth of UVA-adjustable deposits slowed and can impact the price of the dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds became the "ghost" of the region and Argentina. The difference is that neighboring countries devalue their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  while Argentina anchors a dollar that is growing against all the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With this strategy, the country is creating a dangerous \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  arrears. Although soybeans are approaching $530, a low dollar limits \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  income.\par \par \uc2 Of course, faith in the dollar income of the harvest in the short term is what keeps the Economy Minister, \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , standing, enduring the adversity within the ruling party, which are stronger than those imposed on him by a world with volatile markets.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the Government not only went on to sell bonds to contain alternative dollars, but also followed telephone "recommendations" and threats of inspections. In the market they have aimed at a group of traders who must be managed as if they were walking on a minefield when they want to trade with the AL30C, the bond used by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the official square.\par \par \uc2 The dollar exchange operated $27.6 million and rose 76 cents to $145.87 on last financial day last week. The liquidation, which moved $71.7 million, rose 48 cents to $147.73. For the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  there is peace of mind as long as these dollars, which are the ones influencing inflation, do not exceed $150. But, if you look deeper and go to the market where you trade with the GD30, the liquidation account went up $1.70 to $151.70 and is sending signals that the buying trend is strong and has a direct relationship to the liquidation of exporters who, with the pesos that pay them for their dollars, go to this market to buy the so-called "flight dollar" to cover themselves. And in the mean time, the Central keeps it under control, they're happy because they're taking refuge in a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a lower price than imagined.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, exporters liquidated US$252 million in the wholesale square. Central continued to hold power and allowed the dollar to raise just 9 cents to $90.39. In the week he devalued the peso 56 cents. If this is projected throughout February it gives a devaluation of $2.50 (+2.78%) lower than expected inflation of at least one point. This liquidation allowed him to buy $70 million, but the reserves rose $18 million to $39,803 million because \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the plaza alternative dollars brings him a portion of what he buys.\par \par \uc2 That's why exporters are rushing to liquidate their stocks, before entering the new harvest, to make weights and dollars. Those who are on the tightrope for this situation are the bonds that are indexed by the official exchange rate (linked dollar). In the week they lost almost 5% and there are companies, which are convinced that the exchange rate delay will continue and indebtedly issue linked dollar bonds within 24 to 36 months. Of course, they must be covered by future dollar, which is at ever lower prices. Today the dollar's year-end rate is less than half that they had in October and November last year and does not reach 40% per annum.\par \par \uc2 The "blue" or free dollar, nor is it talked about. It's at $144 with no movement and plenty of vendors. It's a market, too tight to influence the economy. His fame comes from the past where he had so much movement, which became the cause of a court case against the current vice president of the nation because the futures market was used to prevent the "blue" ups.\par \par \uc2 But most importantly, it's what can happen this week. According to the latest central data, the growth of UVA-adjustable deposits is slowing because they see that inflation can fall and the dollarClimb. Those who were lucky enough that these deposits, which have to remain in the bank for 90 days, won in the past week, did not renew them. And those who have it pray that inflation will continue to outperigh the performance of fixed-term rates, alternative dollars, and blue dollars.\par \par \uc2 That is why Argentina now lives on the slopes of markets abroad. \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds had a sharp fall Friday that raised their rate to 1.55 percent, tripled the rate it had nine months ago. But as Argentine bonds fell more than U.S. securities, the country's risk rose to 1,593 basic points, a record that brings it closer to an unpleasant ceiling of 1,600 points and puts bonds with default quotes in the alert zone.\par \par \uc2 Overnite markets operating from 7.30am to opening of stock exchanges around the world are a preview of what can happen because investors place short bets on the future there. In the case of the New York Stock Exchanges, the future at midnight indicated that the Dow Jones is .0.19% up, but the S&P 500, the largest of the indicators, lost 0.04% and the \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  of technology, 0.64%. The bags were closer to opening low than going up.\par \par \uc2 This volatility caused gold to record gains of 0.68%, while oil rose on average by 2.60%. Oil stocks now replace technology stocks in investor favoritism. Soybeans can give good news for Argentina because it rose in Chicago by 1.51% and could exceed the ceiling of $430.\par \par \uc2 The country must be covered by what is happening abroad, because within the Brazil region it is the most affected and has to defend the real from the advance of the dollar with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But every time \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main client devalues, it creates a problem for it.\par \par \uc2 READ ON:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars but can't hold them to grow its reserves\par \par \uc2 The market accepts the dollar anchored by controls, but bets on higher inflation\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210308eh380029c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
