\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Five reasons why Argentine country risk rose to its highest level in more than two months\b0\par\par\uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Foreign dollar bonds resumed the bearish path on the last wheels and yesterday country risk reached 1,461 points, the highest figure since November 2 last year. Even Argentine country risk is now about 300 points higher than it did in early September, when the brand new government securities issued by debt restructuring with private creditors came to market.\par \par \uc2 This securities redemption, for more than $100 billion, was the most successful achievement in the management of Minister \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , in a 2020 plagued by bad news, with GDP falling to about 10 percent.\par \par \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 's country risk index measures the spread of the rate of return on \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  bonds (a very secure asset) with its emerging similar ones.\par \par \uc2 1) Uncertainty over economic policy:\par \par \uc2 Behind the increase in country risk is the perception of investors from abroad, who see with distrust the economic future of Argentina, with a high fiscal deficit and the possible continuity of restrictions in the face of the advancement of the Covid-19 cases. If after three years of recession the economy does not return to a persistent path of growth, fiscal solvency to deal with debt payment from 2023 will also be weakened.\par \par \uc2 "The lack of a credible economic plan, uncertainty about negotiations with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , a regrowth of Covid-19 cases, and new restrictions are the main reasons for this correction, while emerging markets and Brazil take advantage of the tailwind and the value of their assets grew considerably," Said Portfolio Personal Investments.\par \par \uc2 2) Need according to the \uc2 IMF\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 The Argentine Government negotiates with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) an Extended Facilities Agreement, a package usually given to countries experiencing a balance-of-payments crisis. Argentina seeks to postpone the return of disbursements made during 2018 and 2019 for about USD 44 billion, which expire between 2022 and 2023. The agency, in return, calls for an economic programme that includes reforms that balance public accounts.\par \par \uc2 A GMA Capital report stressed that "Argentina could find a trend change with an agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ," while "advances linked to an understanding with the Fund could be more effective in lowering country risk from the current 1,400-point zone and giving renewed momentum to fixed income and stocks."\par \par \uc2 Country risk had fallen to the 1,100-point zone in September, following debt redemption, now the October highs are approaching, when it touched 1,500\par \par \uc2 Research for Traders experts also warned of weakness in Argentine fixed income "mainly because of growing mistrust of the future of the domestic economy, and in a context where the Government negotiates with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  a credit of extended facilities."\par \par \uc2 "We hope that the pace of meetings, all virtual, will accelerate in the coming weeks," IMF spokesman \uc2 Gerry Rice\uc2  said on Thursday. He added that it shared the view of the Argentine authorities that the country needed a carefully balanced set of policies to promote stability, restore confidence, protect the most vulnerable and lay the foundations for sustainable and inclusive growth.\par \par \uc2 3) External volatility:\par \par \uc2 With the announcement of a multibillion-dollar fiscal stimulus plan by US President-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds were re-operated and return rates returned to their highest level in ten months.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year Treasury bond now yields about 1.1% per annum and this increase in US debt spreads to a rise in U.S. premiumsemerging countries, with amplified impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sovereign titles.\par \par \uc2 4) Official \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and regulations of public bodies in the stock exchange dollars (MEP and liquidation) market also affect dollar bond valuations: if they fall, the rate of return rises and country risk increases.\par \par \uc2 The ban on privateers from buying more than $100,000 nominal per week of sovereign bonds, in particular the Bonar 2030 with Argentine law (AL30) - which is used by public bodies to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  the market through mass sales - forces investors to come to other securities. The chosen one is the Bonar 30 with New York Law (GD30), which when liquidated by investors to make dollars, falls into its hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quote.\par \par \uc2 5) Doubts about corporate debt:\par \par \uc2 This week \uc2 YPF\uc2  creditors rejected a $6.2 billion oil bond restructuring plan. As a state-owned company, this lack of dollars to honor commitments abroad was assessed by market operators as a negative factor in the weighting of sovereign securities.\par \par \uc2 On 15 September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  established that it will provide companies with only 40% of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  they require to write off debts abroad and the rest will have to deal with their own holdings or restructure their liabilities.\par \par \uc2 In mid-October, partial relief was provided for firms with debt incurred abroad. The BCRA announced that it will allow firms with debts over $1 million to use export \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cancel them, although companies must report each spin greater than $50,000.\par \par \uc2 I kept reading:\par \par \uc2 Markets: bonds remain low and country risk rises to a peak of November\par \par \uc2 Dollar today: free quote yields to 159 pesos\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  breathes: soybeans, gap and reserve purchases allay fear of imminent devaluation\par \par \uc2 Distortion of new controls raised country risk and all dollar quotes outside the official market\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210115eh1f002k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
