\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Argentine  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  in informal square gains 46 pesos in 11 exchange sessions: operators\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 November 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 (Adjust title and add last paragraph)\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Nov 10 (Reuters) - The Argentine peso in the marginal exchange market maintained its price recovery on Tuesday and narrowing the gap in front of the interbank square, in line with the Government's commitment not to finance themselves with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) funds, operators said.\par \par \uc2 The informal or 'blue' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciated 1.34% daily, at 145/149 per dollar, compared to an all-time low of 195 pesos for the sale scored on 23 October, with an exchange gap against the official market of 87.56%.\par \par \uc2 From the record floor, the weight also called 'parallel' accumulates a strong improvement of 30.87%, equivalent to 46 unit weights.\par \par \uc2 In this way, the buy and sell values of the marginal square are located in the range of the stockweight 'Counted with Settlement' (CCL).\par \par \uc2 "The blue is being rearranged based on the signals sent by the government. It is a very 'small' market, with little volume, but it is always the reference that Argentines have," said one operator on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 At the height of the exchange rate square, the gap almost reached 150%.\par \par \uc2 Argentines tend to cover themselves in this small market in the face of exchange rate restrictions prevailing since the BCRA and the high inflation that takes away purchasing power from the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Argentina will seek in negotiations with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) a program of extended facilities to renegotiate its debt by about $44 billion, in another sign to calm the exchange-change turbulence.\par \par \uc2 The wholesale peso closed on Tuesday with a slight depreciation of 0.10%, at 79.43/79.44 units, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the BCRA.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been mired in an economic crisis since 2018 and is on its way to its third consecutive year of recession, with a contraction of about 12% in 2020, impacted by COVID-19.\par \par \uc2 (Report by Jorge Otaola and Walter Bianchi)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201110egba007n3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
