\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina's exchange pressures moderated by million-dollar asset tender\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, 27 Oct (Reuters) - Argentine peso in alternative markets, given the current restrictions on the official market, improved on Tuesday in a financial square that waited for the result of a tender of letters and bonds to absorb circulating and control \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gaps.\par \par \uc2 Operators estimate that the auction would demonstrate how far officialism would manage to regain some financial confidence.\par \par \uc2 "Amid versions of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , financial dollars continue to loosen even as operators continue to seek coverage in the current climate of political and economic uncertainty," economist Gustavo Ber said, adding that "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to regulate the pace despite the negative balances of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a small square."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  could request an additional item of money from the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) as part of the country's negotiations with the agency to renegotiate a 2018 agreement, an Argentine official said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 * The interbank peso closed with a faint drop of 0.06%, to 78.30/78.31 for every dollar, thanks to the regulation imposed from the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollars of its reserves, which would have fallen about $75 million on the date, according to operators.\par \par \uc2 * Analysts agree that although BCRA reserves are above $40 billion in total, liquid reserves are below $1 billion, leaving the entity with little room for manoeuvre to sustain the weight.\par \par \uc2 * In other alternative exchange places, the 'Cashed with Settlement' (CCL) stock market improved by 1.4% to 162.7 pesos per dollar and the Electronic Open Market (MAE) 'MEP dollar' appreciated by 2.8% to 152.8 per dollar. These two markets allow you to make dollars legally.\par \par \uc2 * For its part, the weight in the marginal strip recovered a strong 4.97%, to 177/181 units in the face of expectations for the outcome of the bond tender. The exchange gap with the interbank market stood at 131.13%.\par \par \uc2 * Operators commented that the market showed few businesses and lack of important buyers, in a segment that marked a historic floor level of 195 pesos for sale last Friday.\par \par \uc2 * Bonuses in the over-the-counter square averaged 0.4%, where the 'Bonar 2030' market reference bond lost 0.8%.\par \par \uc2 * Argentine country risk as measured by JP bank. Morgan climbed 13 basic points, to 1,458 units at 17,00 local time (2000 GMT), against the 1,083 points scored in September when the index for debt redemption with private creditors was reconfigured.\par \par \uc2 * "Without 'drivers' that encourage the investor to position himself in the Argentine market and with some pressure at the international level, the week began again with falls in the various local financial assets," said the Portfolio Personal Inversiones brokerage.\par \par \uc2 * The S&P; Merval stock index sank by 5.82%, at an average close of 46,707.91 units, against the collapse of 5.55% on Monday when it cut the streak of 16 consecutive wheels with a cumulative hike of 27.27%.\par \par \uc2 (Report by Walter Bianchi and Jorge Otaola)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201027egar007z9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
