\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Fernandez backed Guzman amid  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  crisis\b0\par\par\uc2 828 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Ten years after nestor Kirchner's death, President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  gave several radio interviews on Tuesday to remember his friend and in that framework was consulted by the exchange crisis and possible changes in the Cabinet.\par \par \uc2 As dollar shortages continue to hit the economy, with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gap 130% to 142% (depending on the parallel price taken), the questions pointed to Guzman's role and performance.\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 : My duty is to finish with the task that Nestor began and that Cristina followedFern\u225\'00\'E1ndez denied that he is thinking of changing his economy minister and claimed that Guzman is today the one who officiates with a p\u237\'00\'EDvot in the Cabinet, controlling all the variables: mainly the expenses to start reducing the fiscal deficit.\par \par \uc2 In one of the dialogues, with Metro radio, the head of state argued that he and Guzman are "dealing" with the exchange crisis. The objective, he noted, is to narrow the gap between parallel quotes and the wholesale exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The blue dollar falls to $184, while the market awaits government tenderingThere was nothing said by the head of state about the performance of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, Miguel Angel Pesce, an official who is his personal friend and on whom cried criticism for the new restrictions that were implemented in September.\par \par \uc2 "That gap is generated because there are also operators who move the cash with liquidation. Now... of all these things we are dealing with Martin," the President said.\par \par \uc2 Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez was consulted on whether Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n assumed the role of "super minister" in the Cabinet, having preponderance over the rest of the officials and even the chief ministers, Santiago Cafiero.\par \par \uc2 "No, he's the economy minister and we had a fiscal problem. As needs to be solved, Martin has to take control of the situation and all the variables," Fernandez explained. And then he praised his minister's performance.\par \par \uc2 "Martin is an exceptional minister. He's a boy of unique ability and moral integrity. It has a capability that none of its critics have," he said.\par \par \uc2 He also denied that Guzman is "a term minister" and noted that such statements were only published by the press: "Martin is the minister and period. I have nothing more to say."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the CCL\par \par \uc2 Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez added that the objective of his management is to "have a quiet Argentina" and downplayed the criticisms made today by those who were officials of the government of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There is a government that left the country as it left it. Now they explain for themselves how we have to put reserves together. The same people who put the trap at $200 now explain how to get the trap out. They're wonderful," the President ironized.\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 , on \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2 's letter: "It's definitely in support of the government"When asked about the exchange rate crisis, Fernandez said that the blue dollar "is a black market" in which "informality is the rule" and in which "infinity of things" occur, which is basically nourished by the dollars left by foreigners.\par \par \uc2 Later, in an interview with Radio 10, Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez criticized those who speculate on the value of the dollar at a time when the pandemic deepened the economic crisis and opined that "there are those who want a bi-member \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 In this regard, it defended \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the financial and stock market to curb the loss of weight value to the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and did not brazen that strategy from continuing.\par \par \uc2 "We have to be calm to solve this. There's a game ofpressures, and as Cristina said, there are those who want a bi-monthly Argentina. There's no room for speculators. Governing, many govern, but in pandemics we are very little," he said.\par \par \uc2 Fernandez argued that his government is not going to let them "do whatever they want" with the dollar. "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the liquidation count so they understand that they can't do what they want. If we have to step in again, we're going to do it," he said. He added: "We have to allocate dollars to produce, to give work, to export."\par \par \uc2 "We're not going to let them do what they want and we hope they understand, it's not possible for them to act the way they act. As Cristina said, many see the dollar as a savings and treasurer option, but we need the dollars to produce, give work and export," Alberto Fernandez said.\par \par \uc2 POLICY SYNTHESIS Exclusive information and the best analysis, on Mondays in your mail. Enter your email Send Thank you for subscribing! An error has occurred, please try again later. We have something to offer youWith our digital subscription you will enjoy more than 300 exclusive items per month and ship our sites without limits. We have premium newsletters, an exclusive community for you, discounts with Club La Voz and more.\par \par \uc2 I want to subscribe from $30 Advertising\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201027egar006hv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
