\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina's assets close with hedge improvements over peso depreciation\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, 8 Oct (Reuters) - Argentina's bonds closed with slight improvements on Thursday, following a bearish start, while stocks strengthened their upward trajectory in the face of speculative portfolio recompositions given the persistent depreciation of the peso in the absence of a clear economic plan, operators said.\par \par \uc2 They added that market interest now focuses on the activity of an International Monetary Funds (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) mission visiting the country to begin laying the groundwork for the renegotiation of a $44 billion credit in 2018.\par \par \uc2 "There are currently no positive signs that can bring about a change in pessimistic market expectations, which is reflected in lower turnovers," said Portfolio Personal Investments (PPI).\par \par \uc2 The Government launched a package of measures a week ago to revive the economy, mainly with the transitional reduction in soybean and derivatives withholdings that may encourage exports, although expected results are not met according to analyst consensus.\par \par \uc2 "In \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with a run of regulations and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the government threw overboard the mood improvement it had achieved with the delayed but successful debt redemption" for about $100 billion with private holders, said Christian Reos, analyst at the brokerage Allaria Ledesma and Compa\u241\'00\'F1\u237\'00\'EDa.\par \par \uc2 * Bonuses in the over-the-counter market ended with a faint average improvement of 0.1%, where the reference 'Bonar 30' rose by 0.8%, in a place that accumulated a decrease of 4.2% in the last five business days.\par \par \uc2 * Traders note that the high dollar yields offered by local bonds, in a 14% and 15% tone, do not attract investors for risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 * Country risk developed by JP bank. Morgan was down 15 units, to 1,358 basic points, to 17,00 local time (2000 GMT), away from the 1,297 units with which he closed the previous month.\par \par \uc2 * In the stock market segment, the leading S&P; Merval index improved by 1.66%, at an average close of 45,482.18 points, accumulating a 10.23% improvement in the last six business sessions with financial stocks leading the trend.\par \par \uc2 * "Local assets continue to reflect investor caution, while continuing to monitor exchange rate dynamics on a daily basis, as it is the most urgent imbalance to resolve in the short term, as well as fiscal and monetary policy signals that may come from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's mission," one economist said.\par \par \uc2 * Wholesale peso fell a faint 0.03% to 77.11/77.13 per dollar, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) regulating the liquidity of the square since opening.\par \par \uc2 "Private market sources estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold between $15 million and $20 million to supply wholesale demand," said Gustavo Quintana, operator of PR Corredores de Cambio.\par \par \uc2 * The monetary entity last week abandoned a daily uniform devaluation scheme to adapt the value of the peso to the rate of depreciation required by the situation.\par \par \uc2 * "In Argentina dollars are missing (...) Net reserves (from the BCRA) drilled $7 billion and liquid reserves dangerously broke $1 billion. The dynamics then became unsustainable and \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  reinforced the trap in the middle of last month, even at the cost of increasing the gap and uncertainty," said consultancy Ecolatina.\par \par \uc2 * In other \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  alternatives, the 'Liquidation Count' (CCL) of the stock market square operated at 153.1 pesos per dollar, in the Electronic Open Market (MAE), the so-called 'MEP dollar' was traded at 140.6 units, and in the marginal strip, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  marked a new historical minimum level of 158 per dollar and a gap of 104.85%.\par \par \uc2 (Report by Walter Bianchi,Additional report by Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Nessi, Edited by Jorge Otaola)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201008ega800a1e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
