\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 U.S. called for "dismantling" the bait to the dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States government\uc2  hopes that Argentinawill be able to"dismantle" restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and other activities of interest to Argentina's investors, understanding that regulations adopted in a crisis context such as that deepened by the coronavirus pandemic are understandable, although it insists that they have a clear end date to improve the business climate.\u160\'00\'A0\par \par \uc2 Kevin O'Reilly, theman in charge of conducting Washington's relationship with the South American region, was expressed in two colloquies organized on Wednesday by Amcham and the American embassy in Buenos Aires, respectively. There he insisted on giving clear predictability and rules of play to the private sector.\par \par \uc2 The Deputy Undersecretary of Western Hemisphere Affairs of the Department of State presented to investors, entrepreneurs, officials and journalists "an American look" about the "possibilities of the region and Argentina",just as the government attempts to disarm what it has defined as a malicious campaign to extend the widespread conception that a mass exodus of local market companies is taking place.\par \par \uc2 O'Reilly is the same official who visited the country in January to meet with The Minister of Economy, \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 ,and other businessmen who had doubts - like his government - about some erquivocal signals given by President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  on the external front, and who were accentuated this week by the rejection of the report on human rights violations in Venezuela by the Argentine ambassador to the OAS, Carlos Raimundi. The situation caused a scoup and the Chancellery, unofficially, came out at the crossroads saying that Raimundi - leader of the Solidarity Party, linked to Carlos Heller- overstepped his bounds and expressed personal opinions that do not represent the state.\par \par \uc2 Poverty climbed to 40.9% in the first halfCoto to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionWhile\b0 \highlight\uc2  O'Reilly underlined good understanding with \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  and vowed to continue developing the bilateral link, while supporting dialogue with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ). Do not ostate, the U.S. stated that his government expects that "during the course of Argentina's economic recovery it will offer a greater investment climate that allows and that short-term measures, aimed at putting limits on private activity, will disappear."\par \par \uc2 O'Reilly addressed the access and mobilization restrictions on assets introduced a few days ago to curb pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar and reserve quotes, and demanded "market competition rules" and "a level court for all."\par \par \uc2 "When Minister \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  talks about taking transitional measures to surf the crisis, we respect them as part of a democratic government. The transition period is difficult to determine, and I understand that the added pandemic on the whole situation is a huge challenge," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We are confident that Argentina will remain a partner that makes reliable and democratic decisions for its society."\par \par \par \par \uc2 Dead Cow and Telecommunications, in doubtThe undersecretary of state assessed that U.S. companies wanted to invest heavily in energy and infrastructure, and particularly in the development of the vaca Muerta site-linked supply chain. However, it considered that the conditions were not met at the moment.\par \par \uc2 "We are hopeful thatthere are more facilities to finance infrastructure projects later. We were looking hard at the provision of services in Vaca Muerta, and weknow that's complicated now," the American weighed on a sector in which the government is also committed to developing the value chain with local players.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, O'Reilly was forceful in rejecting Decree 690/2020 which declared telecommunications services essential and left the fees to be charged to users in state management.\par \par \uc2 "We hope to compete freely in the expansion of communication networks in Argentina, but that will depend on how Argentina organizes the rules of the sector,"he said. Asked about the UND signed by the president, he considered that it may short-term cause "Argentines and companies to have trouble accessing the innovation and inputs they need to compete in the international market," and insisted, "I hope all this is transient."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200930eg9u008ao\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
