\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Pabl\u243\'00\'F3 Chall\u250\'00\'FA: "The Government aggravated the inherited crisis and created more rigidities"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,892 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Minister of Economy, \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , gave signs as the week averaged, in an event of public works announcement in Chaco, Misiones, C\u243\'00\'F3rdoba, La Pampa and Salta, on what are its objectives, or at least in what model of country you believe: "move towards a quieter and more opportunity economy. Our goal is to be able to give Argentina a productive structure that satisfies five conditions: that it is inclusive, that generates work, that is dynamic, a country that adds value to its production, an economy that is stable and gives an environment of economic security to Argentines and Argentines, that follows a federal development strategy; that development respects a concept of fairness across the regions of the country, and that respects our sovereignty."\par \par \uc2 However, in a year in which the Government decided to operate without a budget, although as a result of the emergence of COVID-19 asked Congress to expand the 2019 legacy and accept a deficit equivalent to 8% to 10% of GDP, it seems that before expanding the size of the state with the announcement of a Federal Public Works Plan the time calls for the presentation of a comprehensive economic plan that is capable of recreating the trust of private investors.\par \par \uc2 In this line he manifested himself through a column in Infobae Pablo Chall\u250\'00\'FA, economist, former secretary of Interior Trade, as a year before the assumption of the presidency of \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  in an interview with this medium, when he believed that "Peronism is the only one that can get Argentina out of the vicious cycle of stagnation and high inflation".\par \par \uc2 - Why do you think it is not enough for the Government to set out objectives and not to announce an economic plan?\par \par \uc2 - In fact, in no area of life is it possible to achieve goals without explaining how they will be achieved. If this were to happen, we would say that this is a mere expression of desires, meaning that there is no good chance that these objectives will be achieved. When the Government is the one holding such an opinion, we go into trouble, firstly because the plan is needed for all officials to act in the same direction; if they did not exist, or each would expect them to be told how to act or, perhaps worse, they could interpret in their own way how best to achieve them, which would constitute a powerful ferment contrary to the proper functioning of the government.\par \par \uc2 The economic plan is needed for all officials to act in the same direction; if they didn't exist, or everyone would expect them to be told how to act or, perhaps worse, they could interpret in their own way how best to achieve them\par \par \uc2 But economic policy is also the frame of reference in which the activity of entrepreneurs, workers, savers and investors takes place. If they do not know what the Government will do to achieve its objectives, what paths it will follow and which ones it will avoid, then their expectations will be unreferenced and their conduct will only by chance be functional to the proposed objectives so that these can only be achieved by chance.\par \par \uc2 - More than 8 months of management, and beyond the change of scenery that led to the emergence of COVID-19, there are few officials who justify the poor state of the economy by the "inheritance" Does that view share? Is the cause of the deterioration in relative prices: tariffs, exchange rates, a gap between public and private sector wages, and the implosion of unemployment and poverty rates, among others?\par \par \uc2 - Clearly, "inheritance" is one of the causes that explain the crisis facing the economy today. As early as 2019, the economic situation could be described as facing the worst crisis of recent decades. The failure of The Policies of Change, by a misguided vision of thethe global economy and the poor design of economic policy instruments, left the country with imbalances in both its external and public sectors, passing through a virtually broken \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a serious productive, inflationary and relative price crisis.\par \par \uc2 But the current government has done nothing to address these imbalances and put the country on a path of revival and price stability: it has only merely responded to the plight of the lower-income population or some of the companies forcibly stopped. This inaction is largely due to resistance and delays in formulating a plan that simultaneously attacks all the factors involved. In this way, it aggravated the crisis, creating at the same time new rigidities such as the worsening control of changes and the various freezing of prices and tariffs.\par \par \uc2 "The Government has done nothing to address legacy imbalances and put the country on a path of revival and price stability: it has only merely responded to the plight of the lower-income population or some of the companies forcibly stopped"- Are you concerned about the magnitude of fiscal and monetary imbalances? Is it a consequence of the emergence of COVID-19?\par \par \uc2 - These are undoubtedly very worrying imbalances with a fiscal deficit that can be close to 14 points of GDP; a monetary issue that leads the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's liabilities to double in a few months. Comments circulate there, even among government-linked economists, who attribute to the so-called "modern monetary theory" the conclusion that this would have no major problems and that it could therefore be financed unlimitedly by weight issuance, implying not only a serious and dangerous error but also a very bad reading of what theorists who wrote on this subject argue on this subject, implying not only a serious and dangerous error but also a very bad reading of what theorists who wrote on this subject argue on this subject , they never claimed such a thing.\par \par \uc2 However, these ideas seem to have their influence on members of the government who advocate the implementation of an extensive public works plan financed as an instrument to deal with the crisis, to implement, aggravate imbalances and lead to a sharp increase in the risks of a hyperinflationary process.\par \par \uc2 The implementation of an extensive public works plan financed as an instrument to deal with the crisis, to be implemented, would aggravate imbalances and lead to a strong increase in the risks of a hyperinflationary process\par \par \uc2 - How do you imagine the recomposition of the relative prices of the economy?\par \par \uc2 - A recomposition of relative prices can only be achieved within a comprehensive plan covering a social agreement on income policy, with explicit, coherent and effective commitments between the public sector (exchange rate, interest rates, tariffs, taxes), the employer sector (prices) and workers (wages). It would be long to describe the concurrent policies and measures to be adopted, but the central focus must be the productive recovery and a clear trend for persistent downward inflation.\par \par \uc2 - Does the severe deterioration of the social picture limit the Government's ability to face active policies to revive the economy as a whole?\par \par \uc2 - In my opinion, when the Government decides to faceactive policies to revive the economy within an economic plan of simultaneous policies and measures, then the conditions for a sustained improvement of the social picture and the decline of social subsidies will be given.\par \par \uc2 "When the Government decides to face active policies in order to revive the economy within an economic plan of simultaneous policies and measures, then the conditions for a sustained improvement of the social picture and the decline of social subsidies will be met"- Many economists warn that Argentina has long since lost degrees of freedom to order the economy because of the bi-millennial regime that adopted society Does it share this diagnosis? Where do you think you should start to reverse that picture and what effects it would have on the immediate?\par \par \uc2 - Until we accept in all that implies that the problems of the bi-millennial economy are due to the loss of the attribute of our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a reserve of value, that is to say at high and persistent inflation, then we will continue to be subject to the swings, problems and contradictions of having two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; one change, i.e. for everyday transactions, and one of value reserve. The recovery of weight as a reserve of value is difficult to achieve immediately, but a virtuous path can be designed that accelerates times through the generation of favorable expectations, a situation that could occur if it is clear that the economic plan that is implemented quickly leads to lasting price stability.\par \par \uc2 The recovery of weight as a reserve of value is difficult to achieve immediately, but you can design a virtuous path that accelerates times through the generation of favorable expectations, a situation that could occur if you see clearly an economic plan\par \par \uc2 - After several concessions, Minister \uc2 Mart\u237\'00\'EDn Guzm\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  reached an agreement with the bonists under foreign legislation, but fails to recreate confidence in management What measures do you think should be taken to generate certainty?\par \par \uc2 - The principle of agreement with the bonuses and, later, with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , must be celebrated because they basically move the country away from the worst-case scenario that is the default. But these agreements do not solve the macro imbalances of our economy, nor do they lead the country on a path of revival with price stability, objectives in which everything is about to be done. Until this is done we will continue to have high levels of uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 - In an interview I did a couple of weeks before he took over the presidency \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  said: "Peronism has the foundation to deal with problems. It's a moderate policy, a policy of agreements"Do you think the government has these bases?\par \par \uc2 - I continue to argue that Peronism has the basis for the solution of macro-crisis that our country is facing today. And it has them because they are provided by its doctrine that is neither populist nor elitist and that in its objectives of the well-being of the people and the greatness of the Fatherland finds the necessary balance between an economy that privileges production, employment and price stability at the same time as improving income distribution. The government has not defined the office as a Peronist but as a coalition one: so it can have these bases, but so far it has not implemented them.\par \par \uc2 -How does the world see after the pandemic, and how is \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  prepared?\par \par \uc2 - I see a world where nationalist and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions will prevail, where each country will try to maximize its possibilities and where there will be no fixed rules. New international organizations or a modification of existing ones are likely to be required to bring order to situations that may be defed. A difficult and conflicting world, but in which our country will have a better chance of developing autonomous policies.\par \par \uc2 Photos: Gustavo Gavotti\par \par \uc2 I kept reading:\par \par \uc2 Argentina, the second-worst country in an international ranking of economic misery\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 : "We are going to present a realistic 2021 budget, not one that needs to be modified after 10 days"\par \par \uc2 Economic activity needs to be raised by 15% to return to the pre-quarantine level\par \par \uc2 The history of exchange controls: how the gap between the free dollar and the official\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200823eg8n000s7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
