\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real recovers as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 , broader Latam markets sluggish\b0\par\par\uc2 497 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2020\par 21:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Brazilian real gains on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  warns of 'deep debt restructuring' \par     * Chilean peso hit by lower copper prices\par     * Surge in coronavirus cases keeps investors risk averse\par \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Shreyashi Sanyal\par     Feb 13 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real recovered slightly on\par Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market to ease selling pressure, while regional stocks came\par under pressure as the number of coronavirus deaths and\par infections surged in China. \par     The real hit a record low earlier in the session\par before reversing course to trade 0.2% higher at 4.34 per dollar\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $1 billion of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap\par contracts on the spot market, its first \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since late\par November.\par     Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell through 4.38 per dollar to a new low\par on Thursday after a five-day losing run, hit by a series\par downbeat data and lack of overseas demand for the country's\par assets with interest rates at a record low.\par     Latest figures showed services activity in Brazil shrank\par 0.4% in December, suggesting the economy lost steam at the end\par of 2019. \par     "I'm sure many people in Brazil will be happy to see any\par brief relief but the bigger story is that the real is going to\par continue weakening," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Ashbourne\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior emerging\par markets economist at Capital Economics.\par     Latin American stocks took a beating as a surge in the\par number of coronavirus cases and deaths jolted investors who were\par hoping the outbreak would peak soon. As of Thursday, total\par deaths in China from the SARS-CoV-2 virus were 1,367, up 254\par from the previous day.\par     The MSCI index of Latam stocks was down\par about 0.9%, with Argentine stocks dropping 3%.\par     Argentina's Economy Minister Martin Guzman said the\par government was willing to pay its debts but did not have the\par money to do so, warning of a "a deep debt restructuring" ahead.\par \par     The peso weakened against the dollar, while counter\par bond prices fell an average of 2%.\par     The Mexican peso edged up after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut\par its benchmark interest rate for a fifth straight meeting,\par lowering it 25 basis points to 7.0% as expected.   \par \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2018 GMT:\par     \par            Stock indexes                    Latest    Daily %\par                                                        change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                       1105.21      -0.4\par  MSCI LatAm                                  2784.47     -0.94\par  Brazil Bovespa                            115542.39     -0.97\par  Mexico IPC                                 44890.98     -0.99\par  Chile IPSA                                  4659.81     -0.17\par  Argentina MerVal                           38640.30    -3.245\par  Colombia COLCAP                             1654.63      -0.3\par                      