\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina in the way: the stock market and the dollar rose, while stocks collapsed in the world\b0\par\par\uc2 879 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 In banks and exchanges, where the public runs the monthly dollar quota of up to $10,000, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 12 centsArgentina's economy gave a sample of the crisis that lives with behavior that baffled those who do not live in the country.\par \par \uc2 The behavior of the financial market was absurd because it had data that contradicted those on the planet that was in the midst of a stock, bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 The world's stock exchanges and the dollar collapsed hand in the hands of poor figures in the US economy and by the \uc2 World Trade Organization\uc2 's halved forecasts of growth in the economy.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  forcefully to prevent the dollar from rising against the peso and the local stock exchange had a hike of more than 2%. Global stockmarkets, in turn, endured very heavy falls. Wall Street stock markets threaded their second consecutive decline. In those two days they lost almost 4%. Europe's stock market fell by more than 3% and those in Asia were not better off.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, meanwhile, lost 0.15% against the world's top six and yielded 0.70% against the Brazilian real; 0.50% versus Chilean peso and 0.10% compared to Mexican peso.\par \par \uc2 In the local wholesale market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had intense work that led him to participate as a seller from the first minute and that cost him more than $80 million of his reserves. Besides, he was a strong seller of the future. All this artillery made the wholesale dollar unable to exceed the price of $58 and ended with an 18-cent rise to $57.82.\par \par \uc2 In banks and exchanges, where the public runs the monthly dollar quota of up to $10,000, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  went up 12 cents. His rise was no major from the official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollars that \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  cannot control gave the actual version of the lawsuit. The settlement count increased 0.7% to $66.90 and the MEP dollar rose to $63.10. It should be clarified that the price of bonds or dollar shares used to raise capital influences here.\par \par \uc2 The bonds had a nominal hike in pesos below that of the dollar's rise, so their parities fell, causing the country's risk to rise 23 units to 2,182 basis points.\par \par \uc2 For example, the Bonar 2024, the most used title to make "counted with liqui", increased by 0.24% and Bonar 2020, 0.79%. Longer-term dollar securities rose just over 1%. Longer bonds are those that influence country risk. Add to this the strength of \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bonds where investors took refuge in the collapse of the stock exchanges. The rise in US securities caused its yield to drop to 1.59% and this rate was what caused the world's dollar fall. As you know, the higher the price of the bonus, the lower your rate of return.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves lost $146 million despite the slight rise in gold and the euro. They are now at $48.340 million.\par \par \uc2 The eye-catching data was the upsand of the $144 million dollar deposits. This happened last Friday, according to information provided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This is the first time deposits have been raised since 12 September last.\par \par \uc2 In the Liquidity Letters (Leliq) tender, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to lower rates. He placed securities of $246,682 million at 76.99% per annum, implying a rate reduction of 0.77 millionPoints. And because he absorbed more pesos than they won, he took $16 billion out of circulation that will take some pressure off the purchase of dollars.The Stock Exchange, the other absurd chapter of local markets, had a day of surprises. S&P Merval, the leading stock index, increased 2.41% with businesses by $754 million. Banks led the movement. Galicia (+3.68%) and Macro (+3%) were the highlights. \uc2 Transportadora Gas del Norte\uc2  continued to surprise investors. It added up 8.46%.\par \par \uc2 In two days it increased 14.60% and last month it rose 89%. Still, he loses 4.06% in the year. The price of paper had been so low that from the beginning of last month buyers appeared waiting for the sale of the company, or at least know that in the medium term they will more than recover their investment.\par \par \uc2 Source: RavaOn Wall Street, Argentine ADRs - dollar-traded stock holding certificates used to make settlement transactions - had the majority of hikes. Only four ADRs lowered their price. The best performing was Macro with 3.55%, followed by Galicia with 2.90%.\par \par \uc2 For the next wheel, the dollar is expected to continue to rise and the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  exit \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  will advance. The unknown is still the Stock Exchange. How long it'll last this spring. However, the latest moves show that bullish rallies last little and soon a take profit comes.\par \par \uc2 I kept reading:\par \par \uc2 Vidal promised to lower the tax pressure on the camp\par \par \uc2 In front of ruralists, \uc2 Axel Kicillof\uc2  promised "a productive policy that takes into account all sectors" and ruled out land reform\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191003efa30014t\par }\pa