\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The dollar's multiple prices returned to Argentina and analysts see potential risk\b0\par\par\uc2 857 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 GUSTAVO STOCKThe multiple dollar quotes are back in Argentina. Like what happened during the iron exchange rate strain imposed by the government of Cristina de Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner between 2011 and 2015, in the last three weeks the mechanisms to circumvent the restrictions launched on 1 September last were reactivated.In addition to the increase in demand for the parallel dollar or "blue" that is achieved through caves or "trees", legal \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been growing strongly with which you can buy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the capital market, either to leave them in the country or to send them to an account on the outside."In this new change control, the restrictions are basically aimed at companies.\par \par \uc2  That's why companies that want to dollar their portfolios and turn dividends or resources abroad have no choice but to turn to the MEP dollar or the Settlement Spot," says Eric Ritondale, chief economist at the consulting firm Econviews in Buenos Aires.The MEP is the dollar that is obtained through the purchase in pesos of bonds that are then sold in dollars in the local market. The Count with Settlement arises from a similar mechanism, but the difference is that the sale of the bonds or shares is credited abroad, allowing to take away \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the country.Unlike the trap implemented by Kirchnerism, the current controls impact people less. At that time, all individuals who wanted to buy dollars had to go through the Federal Revenue Administration (AFIP) filter first. That discretionary lock limited the purchase of dollars on the official market to the extreme for various purposes, from treasure to trips abroad. This time, however, the new controls allow the purchase of up to $10,000 per month per person without the need to ask for any authorization. In addition, there are no restrictions on accessing dollars for travel or any extra taxes for purchases abroad.Control is much stricter for companies. Companies and institutional investors are prevented from buying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the official market for treasure and can only access dollars on the official market to pay for imports or debt.It is the cost that companies are paying for the value of the dollar to be able to take \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out of the country, as is apparent from the Settlement Counted transactions."Companies are prohibited from transferring profits or dividends abroad, which leads them to become more than through alternative mechanisms taking into account the fear of what will come," says Fernando Baer, associate economist at Quantum Finance in Buenos Aires. "Disarming the current exchange rate scheme of restrictions will necessarily push up the price of the dollar, and those expectations make those who want to have dollars pay a higher price through the available roads," he added.Last Friday, the value of the dollar that resulted from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Counted with Settlement reached 68.29 Argentine pesos. In practice, that means companies prefer to pay 20.5% overcost over the wholesale official exchange rate to$yupuitize their portfolios and place \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  outside the country. The MEP dollar, meanwhile, closed at 65.86 Argentine pesos, 16.2% more than the official exchange rate.With the limitations on the purchase of dollars, the government of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  managed to stabilize the price of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the official market around 57 Argentine pesos and, as important as that, stop the massive withdrawal of deposits from banks. However, analysts focus on the evolution of the gap between the official exchange rate and the rest of the quotes resulting from legal transactions forbuy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "For now, access to the exchange market is not as restricted as in the kirchnerism years, and so there isn't as big a gap as that at the time," Ritondale says. "But if the controls were to intensify, the gap will surely tend to grow to 50%," he added.The likelihood of the bolt being reinforced is tied to the dollar shortage.Although the gross reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Argentine Republic (BCRA) add up to about US$ 50 billion, if they discount, among other items, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap with the Bank of the People's Republic of China, loans with the International Bank of Basel and a portion of the disbursements of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) which is intended only to strengthen stock, net reserves amount to about US$ 13 billion."If the $5.4 billion \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursement that was scheduled for this month is not finally realized, the government is going to have to turn to the BCRA to honor the debt by December," Ritondale says. Treasury maturities add up to $6.5 billion by the end of the year.With ever-increasingly limited firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market, no one in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules out that change control is spinning. "Most likely in the coming weeks we will see hardening of exchange rate restrictions in areas where the BCRA detects that there are more leaks," Baer says.Copyright Grupo de Diarios Am\u233\'00\'E9rica - GDA/El Pais/Uruguay\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190923ef9n00333\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\