\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 : "Without the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , the situation in Argentina would be much worse"\b0\par\par\uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Christine LagardeOutside the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ), the agency's former managing director, \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 , gave an interview to the AFP agency in which she referred to the decision to approve the two stand-by agreements with \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  and assured that, without the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  economic crisis in the country "would be much worse."\par \par \uc2 "What would have happened if we hadn't been there? if we hadn't done anything? I think it would have been a lot worse. For me there is no doubt about this,"said Lagarde, who formally left her post on 13 September and is quick to become the next president of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ). The leading candidate to succeed her in her previous role is Bulgarian economist \uc2 Kristalina Georgieva\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, Lagarde indicated that in June 2018, when the \uc2 IMF\uc2  approved the first salvage - of US$50 billion - Argentina was in a situation of financial isolation where the agency had become the only source of financing international lybere that the country could count on.\u160\'00\'A0"I went that way, I touched the doors of many countries. I received many kind words and gentle supports, but no funding," he said.\par \par \uc2 "When Argentina knocked on our door it was in a particularly difficult situation. We tend to forget about that because everyone is focused on Argentina today,"he added.\par \par \uc2 While Lagarde also stated that even in the early stages of programme implementation, she considered that "there was little chance" of it's stabilizing the economy.\u160\'00\'A0But he emphasized that the work of the entity is to provide support.\par \par \uc2 Three months after the first loan, and after the first loan failed to bring calm to economic players at both the national and international levels, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  expanded the credit to $57 billion: at least as of June 2019, this figure accounted for 61% of total loans provided by the entity around the world.\par \par \uc2 THE MI's drecora, \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 , with Minister Dujovne in announcing the expansion of the Stand-by program. (NA)So far, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  has awarded Argentina a total of US$44 billion. According to the schedule of the agreement, the country would have to have undergone a review of program compliance in September, a condition necessary to unlock the sending of a new fee of USD 5.4 billion.\par \par \uc2 However, the review remained between question marks since \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2 's broad victory in the PASO altered all plans and resulted in 20% further depreciation of the peso by- in the departure of \uc2 Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Dujovne\uc2  who, until then, was the \uc2 IMF\uc2  technicians had in Argentina.\par \par \uc2 The Fund's mission to do this review first delayed his visit to the country and then, when he finally traveled, changed his purpose. It was no longer to analyze the evolution of the numbers of the economy and then to internalize on the plans of the new Minister of Finance, \uc2 Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Lacunza\uc2 , and to meet with \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  and hisTeam.Alberto Fernandez with \uc2 Alejandro Werner\uc2 , director of the IMF's Western Hemisphere Department and Trevor AlleyneDays later, Lacunza announced a willingness to renegotiate the agreement with the Monetary Fund and "reprofile" Argentina's debt. In addition, it introduced a series of exchange rate controls aimed at avoiding a dollar stampede amid uncertainty. In its latest submission, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  referred to these restrictions as "capital flow management measures" aimed at "protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability and savers."\par \par \uc2 The Government will take its next step in search of the new end-of-month disbursement, when Lacunza travels to Washington to meet with the Fund's authorities, led on an interim backdrop by \uc2 David Lipton\uc2 . Authorities of the international body confirmed that the review will be part of the conversation.\par \par \uc2 I kept reading:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  confirmed Minister Lacunza's trip, but gave no details on the $5.4 billion disbursement\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190920ef9k00152\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
