\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina, on the brink of an economic, political and social catastrophe, as in 2001\b0\par\par\uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 ? Food delivery to the unemployed and homeless, in Buenos Aires. The image is file. Photo Reuters Stella CalloniPeri\u243\'00\'F3dico Newspaper Correspondent The DayWednesday, September 4, 2019, p. 27Buenos Aires. With the feeling of being facing an economic, political and social catastrophe, the porte stock market collapsed on Tuesday 11.5 percent, with the most affected roles being those linked to energy companies, which fell more than 15 percent, while the Bank Central \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars directly, which had been prohibited by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ), closing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $58.50 and reserves lost $954 million to 53,144 million.\par \par \uc2 The country risk climbed to 2,536 points, at a time when Nobel Economics Laureate \uc2 Paul Krugman\uc2  compared the situation to the 2001 crisis and held the government and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  accountable.\par \par \uc2 He considered that at the beginning of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's government there was a honeymoon with the markets and then because of the massive support of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , "but in the end all it did was dig a deeper well, with a large increase in external debt and discrediting neolib reformers they were them.\par \par \uc2 What is surprising to those of us who have spent a lot of time in these crises is that this is incredibly close to the script of 1998-2001; with no convertibility law, but still with similar policy errors, and a similar enablement of those errors by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , Krugman wrote on his \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account, and that he was picked up by most media here.\par \par \uc2 He criticized former \uc2 IMF\uc2  incumbent \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 , who was intended to run the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ), who strongly supported the granting of the fund's largest-case loan to Argentina, with $57 billion. This makes me more concerned about Lagarde at the \uc2 ECB\uc2 . Everyone involved really, really should have known.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar came to sell at 59 pesos and the blue (parallel) was offered at 63.50 pesos, closing the gap between the two, while the Merval index collapsed 11.7 percent, its low in two years, led the fall by energy and bank papers , and bonds fell to 9 percent.\par \par \uc2 The BCRA unveiled the August Market Expectation Survey (REM) anticipating that inflation will climb to 55 percent this year with a dollar to 66.70 pesos next December and a benchmark rate of 80 percent this month.\par \par \uc2 The report acknowledges that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  financed capital flight, in a clearly unsustainable process that also violates the principles reflected in its own charter.\par \par \uc2 "The agency's disbursements so far were $44,867 billion, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  outflow \u8211\'20\'13 between those of the formal system and speculative capital \u8211\'20\'13 totals $36,64 billion. The \uc2 IMF\uc2  failed in its projections of GDP developments, inflation, interest rate levels and the volume of international reserves," Financial Scope reported.\par \par \uc2 According to this report, the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's estimated GDP growth was 1.5% and this fell 1.3%; it also forecast inflation of 17 percent, but it's already 54.4 percent. The same government acknowledges, even before the entire loan has been disbursed, that Argentina will have obvious problems in meeting its commitments, the report concludes.\par \par \uc2 Given the seriousness of the social situation, deepened by the brutal devaluation that Macri tries to stop with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  control decreed last Sunday, 50 mayors of the Peronism of the province of Buenos Aires asked in a letter tothe provincial governor, Mar\u237\'00\'EDa Eugenia Vidal, who declares the food emergency and strengthens the budget items received every month by the dining rooms and schools of Bonaerenses.They called for urgent action to mitigate the ferocious impact that economic policy increasingly causes on vast sections of society, highlighting the dire situation our people are experiencing because of the crisis that has deepened in Argentina, with tough implications in that province (Buenos Aires) and demanding that Vidal take responsibility for dealing with the critical situation faced by more and more school-aged children and adolescents and the general population, and they agreed on the need to increase school canteens, and make tax obligations on small traders, suffocated by the crisis, more flexible.\par \par \uc2 By lighting more fires, the Minister of Production and Labour, Dante Sica, admitted that the last steps taken by Macri's management are to have a good electoral result that allows us to go to the second round in the elections on October 27.\par \par \uc2 All the opposition sectors asked the president to leave the election campaign and devote himself to stabilizing the country, which is bordering on default.\par \par \uc2 Sica was confident that the changes made in recent days, which will have to overcome two difficult months, will lead to a good result, even though the presidential candidate of the opposition Frente de Todos, Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez, has between 55 and 56 percent of the in. holding votes on their behalf, according to polls.\par \par \uc2 Argentine Industrial Union\uc2  owner Miguel Acevedo considered that wage negotiations will have to be opened, coinciding with the urgent demand of the trade unions and said that it will cost us 10 years to rebuild the purchasing power of wages especially after the government's determined devaluation of its defeat in the primary.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190904ef94002z0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
