\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Brazil's establishment questioned Macri's latest economic measures and closely follows in the footsteps of Alberto Fernandez\b0\par\par\uc2 801 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro and \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 , smiles before the PASO and the triumph of Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez.\u160\'00\'A0 (Efecdos)ST. PAUL. The word "Argentina", with a crisis that frightens entrepreneurs, investors and politicians, gained space in the caps of the Brazilian news media. Instead, it disappeared from the tweets and the statements of Jair Bolsonaro and his closest collaborators.\par \par \uc2 President Bolsonaro's last comments, a day after the PASO, were derogatory about Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez's Front of All. And days later, on Tuesday, August 27, Vice President Hamilton Mourao worked to "deideologize" bilateral relations.\par \par \uc2 "Argentina is our third largest trading partner and we need to maintain ties with the country. We have to preserve our interests." After this sentence of Vice President Mourao, in Brasilia there were no more official mentions of the Argentine elections.\par \par \uc2 The victory of August 11 led the Brazilian establishment to the conviction that the next Argentine president will be Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez. They see almost no chance of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  getting hisre-election. Hamilton Mourao himself spoke "of strong signs" of an opposition triumph. Now, worries are going elsewhere. They ask: How can the Argentine ravine impact the Brazilian economy?\par \par \uc2 What is most frightening, for now, is the "control of the dollar exit" that is among the measures announced by Minister Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Lacunza and the holder of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 . "This is going to cause difficulties in sending dividends to Brazil by Brazilian firms," foreign trade experts anticipate.\par \par \uc2 Carla Junqueira, of Mattos Engelberg, said: "When a capital is invested in a particular country, it is obvious that the investor is looking for a profit. And if I'm a Brazilian company that I invested in Argentina, I'm going to want to bring the profits to Brazil. The problem is that it now needs authorization from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." He concluded: "The biggest fear of foreign investors in any country is not being able to remit profits abroad."\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez and \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2 , the presidential formula of the Front of All.Brazilian media highlight "the 180-degree turn" in President Macri's positions. The testimonies of specialists cited by the local press coincide on one point: "After criticizing Kirchnerism, Macri ended up pursuing the same policies. And that's for lack of skill in his government."\par \par \uc2 According to the newspaper Estado de Sao Paulo "the Macri measure was a surprise". The medium recalled that the Argentine president "reversed many protectionist practices of his predecessor, \uc2 Cristina Kirchner\uc2 , and now fails to contain the strong outflows of investors and sustain the weight, which went into free fall."\par \par \uc2 He added State of Sao Paulo: "Investors are concerned that once the measures come into force,they will not be able to withdraw the dollars. And this will possibly leave \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  again with aeconomy distorted by government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."Hern\u225\'00\'E1n Lacunza, Minister of Finance. (Gustavo Gavotti)Even more pessimistic is the newspaper O Globo. In its analysis it states that "on the first useful day of the month, the trading dollar trades in Brazil with valorization. It is now at 4.16, which represents a 0.43% advance even at the start of the wheel." The cause: "The consequences of the international trade war (US-China) and the crisis in Argentina pushing for change (in Brazil)".\par \par \uc2 The truth is that the holiday in the United States, for Labor Day, leads for the moment to have investors on the Stock Exchange of St. Paul move cautiously. They closely accompany the capital control unfoldings announced by the Argentine government, with the magnifying glass put into the difficulties of transfers abroad,which will require the approval of the BCRA, and in the limits of buying dollars to $10,000 per month.\par \par \uc2 Of course, it does not only influence Argentine shocks in the rise in the dollar's price relative to the real one. Markets assess the data known on Monday on how Brazilians evaluate the Bolsonaro government. According to a survey of Datafolha published this morning, the presidential figure's disregard climbed from 33% in July to 38% today.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed, on the orders of Economy Minister \uc2 Paulo Guedes\uc2 , to make new direct sales of dollars in financial markets. It's already been delivered $450 million, so far in the day. It is the first time in 10 years that the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has traded cash \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm the mood.\par \par \uc2 As in Argentina, since \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  took over the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following agreements with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I kept reading:\par \par \uc2 Debt renegotiation: Government delays treatment in Congress in the absence of opposition agreement\par \par \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez arrived in Madrid to teach at a university and meet Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez\par \par \par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190902ef92005a8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
