\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Argentine peso logs worst month in history, Latam stocks rise\b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2019\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices; adds milestones and Fitch downgrade; changes\par quote)\par     By Agamoni Ghosh\par     Aug 30 (Reuters) - Argentina's peso slumped on Friday,\par underperforming the broader Latin American markets and recording\par its worst monthly performance ever, after ratings agency\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced it was slashing Argentina's\par long-term credit rating to "junk."\par     The ratings action follows the government's announcement to\par "re-profile" some $100 billion in debt earlier in the week,\par sinking Argentine bonds and igniting worries of a full-blown\par debt crisis for Latin America's third-largest economy.\par \par     Fitch downgraded Argentina to "RD" status - restricted\par default - late on Friday, indicating selective payment default\par on a specific class or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of debt.\par  \par    "While the government's plans could alleviate some of the\par short-term liquidity pressures, implementation risks are high\par and further underscore the lack of policy tools to restore\par market stability," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said in a note. \par     The peso fell nearly 3% on the day and logged its\par worst month ever, down 26.3%, surpassing a plunge of 25.8%\par during the August 2018 monetary crisis.\par     The carnage in Argentine markets started after\par business-friendly President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mauricio Macri\f28 \uc2 \f2  suffered a thumping\par defeat in primaries at the hands of Alberto Fernandez, stoking\par fears that the return of a leftist government could herald a new\par era of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policies. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's MerVal stock index maintained enough\par liquidity to rise nearly 4% on Friday, helped by exporters that\par benefit from a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but has shed nearly 40% through\par the month. \par     The rest of the Latin American markets took comfort from\par U.S.-China trade hopes, with stocks rising\par nearly 2%. \par     Sao Paulo-traded stocks climbed 0.8%, while the real\par  gained 1%. August has been the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakest month\par in four years, exacerbated by market positioning, aggressive\par bets on lower interest rates and the crisis in neighboring\par Argentina. \par     Chile's peso dipped marginally, ending the month over\par 2% lower as falling copper prices have taken a toll on the\par world's top producer of the red metal.\par     Colombia's peso fell 0.2% ahead of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par monetary policy decision. Analysts in a Reuters poll in July\par indicated policymakers will likely hold borrowing costs to boost\par slow growth.\par     Markets in Peru were shut for a local holiday. \par \par  Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1940 GMT\par \par  Stock indexes                        daily %\par                              Latest    change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets        983.99     1.43\par                                       \par  MSCI LatAm                  2598.21     1.68\par                                       \par  Brazil Bovespa            101362.18     0.83\par                                       \par  Mexico IPC                 42440.99     1.46\par                                       \par  Chile IPSA                  4791.96     2.13\par                                       \par  Argentina MerVal           25187.14        5\par                                       \par  Colombia IGBC              12564.26     0.56\par                                       \par                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            daily %\par                                        change\par                               Latest  \par  Brazil real                  4.1364     0.81\par                                       \par  Mexico peso                 20.0279     0.52\par                                       \par  Chile peso                    721.5    -0.17\par                                       \par  Colombia peso               3439.65    -0.11\par  Peru sol                          -        -\par                                       \par  Argentina peso              59.5000    -2.69\par  (interbank)                          \par                                       \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Agamoni Ghosh in Bengaluru\par Editing by Leslie Adler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-30T20:59:17.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190830ef8u03kbh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
