\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken over growth worries, stocks rise\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2019\par 21:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices, adds quote)\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2  reduces 2019 growth target for Mexico \par     * ARS slumps despite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par     * Jump in oil prices lifts stocks in Latam \par \par     By Agamoni Ghosh\par     Aug 28 (Reuters) - Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened\par against a firm dollar on Wednesday as investors shied away from\par riskier bets amid global growth worries, while strong demand for\par oil helped equities in the region rise. \par     Adding to a bout of data signaling global slowdown, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexico's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2 , reduced its projected growth for Latin\par America's second-largest economy for the fifth time in a row for\par 2019 and expects a smaller expansion in 2020.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2  also cut its inflation forecast for the end of 2019\par to 3.2% from 3.7% on the back of growth risks arising from\par global trade disputes and struggling state oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pemex\f28 \uc2 \f2 , whose\par ratings downgrade poses a big threat to the sovereign debt.\par     The Mexican peso shed 0.4%.\par     The Argentine peso closed 3% lower, but managed to\par pare some earlier losses as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $262 million\par of its reserves in five \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aimed at controlling the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall. \par     Worries about \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Argentina\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's ability to meet its\par dollar-denominated debt obligations have increased since the\par peso got trounced by political uncertainty after an Aug. 11\par primary election.\par     The real hovered near 2019 lows. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par president \f28 \uc2 \f2 Roberto Campos Neto\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday that inflation\par in Brazil, a country that once suffered from hyperinflation, is\par on a downward path. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  waded into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on\par Tuesday in a rare sale of dollars after the real slumped to its\par weakest level against the greenback in almost a year and within\par sight of its all-time low.\par     The real has lost about 8% of its value against the dollar\par in August, under pressure from worries surrounding global trade\par and economic growth, with mounting expectations for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to further cut interest rates.\par     "The weakness of the economy makes a 50 bp cut in Selic rate\par at the next \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting in September increasingly\par likely," said analysts from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note. \par     A jump in oil prices supported most stock markets, with\par Brazil's Bovespa and Colombian equities gaining\par between 06% and 0.8%. \par \par  Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1930 GMT  \par  Stock indexes                                   daily %\par                           Latest                  change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets              965.33          0.08\par                                             \par  MSCI LatAm                        2505.73          0.77\par                                             \par  Brazil Bovespa                   98081.48          0.83\par                                             \par  Mexico IPC                       40989.16          0.84\par                                             \par  Chile IPSA                        4600.19          -0.1\par                                             \par  Argentina MerVal                 25356.48         2.981\par                                             \par  Colombia IGBC                    12467.15           0.6\par                                             \par                                                         \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                       daily %\par                                     Latest        change\par  Brazil real                        4.1563         -0.53\par                                             \par  Mexico peso                       20.0775         -0.40\par                                             \par  Chile peso                          722.3          0.03\par                                             \par  Colombia peso                     3473.05         -0.17\par  Peru sol                            3.401         -0.24\par                                             \par  Argentina peso                    57.8000         -3.10\par  (interbank)                                \par                                             \par  \par \par  (Reporting by Agamoni Ghosh in Bengaluru\par Editing by Chris Reese)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-28T20:57:58.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190828ef8s03ls9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
