\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Reserves already down $9.5 billion in August: the 7 causes behind the collapse\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  (Maximiliano Luna)In the midst of the crisis that untied among investors following the RESULT of the PASO, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves suffered a drastic decline, which threatened at least to remain or even accelerate in the coming weeks. Stock closed on Friday at $58.259million, but with a risk of a sharp decline in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The phenomenon, which is one of the main reflections of the level of market mistrust in Argentina, is monitored daily by the bCRA owner, \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 . Obey not one but multiple causes. At some point you can see the fall in reserves as the counter-face of the government's need to avoid another spike in the dollar's price in the pre-election and perhaps after the election as well.\par \par \uc2 In August alone, the fall in reserves already exceeds USD 9.5 billion, with a level ending Friday at $58.2 billion. Presidential candidate Alberto Fernandez suggested the need to "take care" of reservations, but this desire is in the way of a major obstacle. It would be difficult not to use them if at the same time it is intended to control a new exchange rate jump following the devaluation that led to the dollar from $46 to $55 in the wholesale market after the August 11 primary election. Much more considering that anxiety will increase as the election approaches.\par \par \uc2 Central BankSpecifically, what is behind this accelerated loss of reserve level? The seven main reasons are as follows:\par \par \uc2 Debt maturities: This is the main target of \uc2 IMF\uc2  disbursements, which originally led Argentina to ask For financial assistance from Washington. All capital and interest maturities are paid on the Fund's loan, with the consequent impact on reserves. It is within the terms of the agreement and has been fulfilling the various obligations month by month. However, the debt repayment failed to restore investor confidence and markets remain closed to voluntary financing for \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of theCentral: after the STEPS, the institution that chairs \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  began selling dollars directly to supply more supply to the market and stop the escalation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It had not done so until now, as it had been softening exchange rate movements with futures sales and raising the interest rate. These sales are directly reflected in the reserve stock.\par \par \uc2 Treasury Dollar Sale: As part of the negotiation reached with the agency earlier this year, an agreement was reached for the Treasury to sell $60 million daily through tenders, until the end of the year. In this way, efforts were made to supply the market with a constant supply of dollars to avoid abrupt fluctuations in the exchange rate. This objective had been achieved in a reasonable way, until the result of the STEPS caused a big jump in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Not Letes renewal: it is also linked to the need to pay the debt. But in this case, as these were short-term maturities, dollar debt renewal had been adequately met. It is possible that in the nextTuesday's tender will only get a partial renewal of the $900 million in Letes that are held by the private sector. If so, the Treasury will have to pay with dollars that are deposited in the BCRA. Until the end of the year, the maturity of these very short dollar securities amounted to up to USD 6.5 billion.Return of a loan to banks: it happened in the last week. The fall in bonds prompted a clause that allowed a consortium of six international entities to apply for the repayment of a loan granted for the purpose of strengthening reserves. The cancellation of the "repo" (loan against bond guarantee) caused in the middle of last week a decrease of USD 2.6 billion in the stock of reserves of the Central.\par \par \uc2 Fall of dollar deposits: There are few economists discussing the desirability of accounting as reserves of the fittings that banks make in the Central of fixed terms in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  made by individuals and companies. Clearly these are \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that belong to savers and cannot be used by the BCRA. Since the result of the STEPS, some US$2 billion has come out of the banks, approximately 6% of the total hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits. Banks have plenty of liquidity to cope with that exit, but it is reflected in reserve reduction.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  oscillation: as part of the reserves is found in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , any quote change has an impact on stock. This was noted mostly in July, when the yuan's devaluation in the face of China's trade war with the United States marked a drop of nearly $300 million. This was a one-off fact, but it reflected the effect of a weakening of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yuan or eventually the euro on reserves.\par \par \uc2 KEEP READING:\par \par \uc2 What Alberto Fernandez economists say when they talk privately with entrepreneurs and bankers\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190826ef8q00234\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
