\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Economist close to Alberto F. calls for review of \uc2 IMF\uc2  deal by December\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Emmanuel Alvarez Agis, former deputy minister of \uc2 Axel Kicillof\uc2  and close to Alberto Fernandez, called for accelerating the renegotiation of the deal with the Monetary Fund. The economist, who this week shared a talk with former \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President (BCRA) Luis "Toto" Caputo, noted that the next step by the economy minister should be to travel to the United States to bring a new agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and whether it can be reviewed before December, they must do it. He also praised \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 's work this week during the exchange rate run.\par \par \uc2 Agis called for an urgent review. "If the agreement has any point where the \uc2 IMF\uc2  says it needs to be reviewed, it needs to be reviewednow. Because the economy cannot transit without an agreement with the IMF untilDecember, it is very important that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  confirms that it will disburse the money it has to disburse and at the same time it says, we have effectively wrong again with the economy Argentina and we're going to review our model."\par \par \uc2 "Thenext economy minister's first step is to take a plane toWashington. And the second will not return in 10 minutes with a non-serving agreement, as has been going on here with the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ," Alvarez Agis said in dialogue with Mitre's "Early Saturday" program.\par \par \uc2 "Anything done in the economy needs the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's endorsement because the only strong financial challenge the Argentine economy has is to return the stand by," the economist said. What has happened with the agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  is that we have complied with it to the letter and here we are: with the exchange rate at $60, with inflation above 50% and with the economy falling for the third time in two years in a new recessionary cycle. It has to be restructured, reformulated."\par \par \uc2 In turn, Agis plotted his diagnosis of the errors of the current agreement. "On monetary policy, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  only in April this year understood what the real conflict of the Argentine economywas: a monetary policy that was very inadequate in the first version of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which was worse when it put us in that area of no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that only in April he understood that \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed the discretion to be able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market. And fiscally, it seems to me that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  has to understand that it is drowning the Argentineeconomy, which is in recession and which cannot continue to be asked for these levels of adjustment because all we are going to do is deepen the recession."\par \par \uc2 "The only goal we have with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which is the fiscal goal, with this level of recession, we will break in in December. In September, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  has to endorse the last quota for this year, and monetary targets, with this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slump, are sure to go into crisis. The \uc2 IMF\uc2  is going to come and overhaul the economy and the first thing you have to understand is that the agreement is not down because the government violated it, the agreement is down because it was misconfigured and there the responsibility is shared: half the government and half the \uc2 IMF\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Alvarez Agis was critical of the latest government measures and praised \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 's work at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with whom Alberto F.'s economic team already has dialogue. "In this context I would have to take three measures: control thedollar, control the dollar and control the dollar. Taking steps to alleviate a situation you still don't know how serious it is is is a mistake. And it can feed back the phenomenon of financial instability," the economist said close to the Front of All presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 "The President with the statements of Sunday and Monday put all Argentines at risk andgenerated a very complex financial situation. The action that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had on Monday and all week was impeccable. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted very professionally because if they went out on Monday to stop the devaluation and sold US$ 1.5 billion, we were on the scene of Sturzenegger in 2018, when it rifed US$1500 million, that signaled that the crisis was very strong , that the BCRA couldn't stop it, triggered the demand for dollars and started to leave it unreserved," he concluded.Ne\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190817ef8h003af\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
