\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina will increase sale of dollars\b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Monetary Policy Committee (Copom) of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Argentine Republic (BCRA) announced that the entity may make sales of dollars even if the exchange rate is below 51.44 Argentine pesos -the current ceiling of the non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone (ZNI) -, whose amount and frequency will depend on market dynamics.\par \par \uc2 In addition, if the exchange rate is above 51.44, the BCRA will increase from 150 to 250 million dollars the amount of the daily sale stipulated so far. Likewise, it may determine the performance of additional \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counteract episodes of excessive volatility if deemed necessary.\par \par \uc2 "We have many \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanisms, the auction is going to be one of them," they said from the BCRA to El Cronista.\par \par \uc2 They also clarified that "within the zone, the amounts and frequency of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are decided by the BCRA and outside the zone the amount becomes $ 250 million, with the possibility of determining additional \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if considered."\par \par \uc2 To this, we must add the 60 million Treasury that are auctioned daily for account and order of the Treasury in two daily tranches of 30 million. In mid-April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its decision to freeze the ZNI with a floor of 39.75 and a ceiling of 51.45 pesos, so it stopped updating daily to remain fixed until the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 The decision was adopted "due to the increase in exchange rate volatility observed in recent days," which caused the dollar to advance 9% last week and to surpass 47 pesos, while the country risk jumped above 1,000 points.\par \par \uc2 The chief economist of Eco Go, Federico Furiase, said in a dialogue with El Cronista that the measure "reinforces discretion in the face of high volatility."\par \par \uc2 "It can help in the very short term, but if the pressure continues it can be a double-edged sword, given the limit of freely available reserves in a context of market closures.\par \par \uc2 "The loss of credibility is a key issue, the demand for money is very weak and inflation expectations are increasing. Increasing nominal adjustment of the exchange rate is required to maintain the real exchange rate, "he said.\par \par \uc2 The Copom considered that the BCRA "should reinforce the contractionary bias of monetary policy, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market to reduce more aggressively the amount of pesos and in this way contribute to the proper functioning of said market".\par \par \uc2 The BCRA will increase from 150 to 250 million dollars the amount of the daily sale stipulated so far. "These \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take place both within what had been defined so far as ZNI, and outside it," the bank said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 "In all cases, the amount of pesos resulting from these sales will be discounted from the monetary base goal. "In this way, the measures allow the absorption of liquidity of pesos when the exchange rate is below 51.44 pesos and intensify this absorption when the price of the dollar is located above," he added.\par \par \uc2 Fund backs BCRA announcement Measures are adequate for Argentina's challenges: IMF Minutes after known the decision of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCRA) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market still within the zone of nonintervention, that is, below 51.44 pesos, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) came out to support the measure .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Argentina\uc2  today introduced important measures to address the recent volatility of the financial market and the type ofchange.\par \par \uc2 "We support these measures, which are adequately calibrated for the challenges facing Argentina," said \uc2 Gerry Rice\uc2 , the agency's chief spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which advocated at all times a flexible exchange rate for Argentina within the standby program agreed to three years with the country, marks an important shift in its vision.\par \par \uc2 "With the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , we talk all the time. In fact, the decision to leave the roof of the band fixed went through 1 million iterations before, "said a government source. "It's a program of high volatility, you know. Now, what is the one that can be admitted and what is the balance between discretion and action, is evaluated on a daily basis, "he added.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the ideological position of the \uc2 IMF\uc2  on the free exchange rate, using the dollars that the agency lends to stop a run and that vanish and end up in the mattresses of the country is what they did not want to happen. Therefore, until today it was the refusal to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190430ef4u0013o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
