\par\par \b \uc2 Argentina to freeze peso trading band until year-end -c. bank head\b0\par\par\uc2 138 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 April 2019\par 22:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, April 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  will freeze a non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band for its peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the end of the year, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  said during a news conference on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The band, which came into effect last year and previously had gradually depreciated, will be set between 39.75 pesos and 51.45 pesos per U.S. dollar, Sandleris said.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's inflation rate accelerated to 4.7 percent in March, data released earlier on Tuesday showed, raising pressure on the country's leaders to protect the peso, which lost almost half its value against the dollar last year.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Eliana Raszewski in Buenos Aires Writing by Adam Jourdan Editing by Matthew Lewis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-4-16T21:35:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190416ef4g03p9a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
