\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Why did the dollar jump in Argentina and what will Uruguay do?\b0\par\par\uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar jumped yesterday in Argentina after the rise in global level that had and approached the record level in that country. Uruguay was no stranger to these events and the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose yesterday. "Beyond that this time the world dusted off more cautiously, domestic assets continue to be immersed in an adverse dynamic, which is still dominated by the growing electoral uncertainty and the economic vulnerabilities that the country has been going through," said Gustavo Ber, economist at Estudio Ber. "The international nervousness contacted the development of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local market, stimulating a dollarization of portfolios," said Fernando Izzo, operator of ABC Mercado de Cambios. In Argentina, the dollar rose 1.83% to close at 41.80 Argentine pesos. So far this year accumulates a growth of 10.88%. In Uruguay, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rose yesterday (for the third consecutive day), 0.76% and quoted at a new historic high: $ 33,616.\par \par \uc2  The new maximum is given since the Uruguayan peso began circulating on March 1, 1993, as a national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , beyond which it is an anecdotal fact (since economically it does not imply anything for the long period that has elapsed). "The dollar today (for yesterday) rose around the world in an important way: The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's announcement (to keep rates throughout the year), which in theory should be an element that weakens the dollar, has had the effect to rekindle the demand for dollars due to economic agents' fears of a recession or abrupt slowdown Today (yesterday) there was a strong fall in the manufacturing production index of Germany, which is the engine of Europe, and this has caused the dollar as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been strengthened, "the president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BCU), Alberto Gra\u241\'00\'F1a, told El Pais as part of an interview. Furthermore, "in the case of Argentina and Brazil (the rise) is exacerbated by the idiosyncratic problems that these countries have" that "in the case of Brazil, the news from the political front -which question the viability of the pension reform- they do not generate stability, "he said. Yesterday in Uruguay, the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to the interbank level between $ 33.50 and $ 33.67 to close at $ 33.59. To the public in the slates of Banco Rep\u250\'00\'FAblica (BROU), the dollar rose 22 cents to purchase and sale, reaching $ 32.90 and $ 34.30, respectively. Through the screens of the Electronic Securities Exchange (Bevsa) 55 transactions were made to negotiate US $ 17.33 million. The BCU remained without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, as in the previous sessions, with 12 sessions without the participation of the Central of the 14 that had so far this month. Regarding what happened yesterday in \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  and if the BCU will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Gra\u241\'00\'F1a was blunt: "We will not react based on events that occur in Argentina, unless they had a direct impact, which we do not see that is the case, in Uruguay some specific channel, we do not see that this is the case at this juncture. " "But, having said that, we have to keep a close eye on what happens in Argentina, Brazil and, ultimately, around the world," he added. The president of the BCU remarked that "this one-day or short-term episode does not merit, in a situation like Argentina's, a (political) response from us." In the week, that is to say with respect to last Friday, the dollar rose 0.5% in Uruguay. So far this month has accumulated an increase of 2.96% and so far this year of 3.79%. In Brazil, the main reference market in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the US dollar ended at 3.8815 reais with an increase of 2.23%. With respect to the end of last year, the variation is 0.15%. Globally, the dollar fell yesterday against the yen, but rose against the euro, as weak manufacturing data in the United States generatedworries about the global economy, while Treasury yields pointed to growing fears of a recession.> This "helps reinforce the idea that we are seeing a slowdown more significant and more widespread than the markets had anticipated a few months ago, "said \uc2 Karl Schamotta\uc2 , director of exchange rate strategy at Cambridge Global Payments. "What we are seeing is a kind of recognition that the Fed is reacting to deeper risks in the global economy," he added.\par \par \uc2 Copyright Grupo de Diarios Am\u233\'00\'E9rica - GDA / El Pais / Uruguay\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190325ef3n001pw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
