\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Argentina seeks market makers to help stabilize the peso - sources\b0\par\par\uc2 385 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 18:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds picture)\par \par \uc2 By Eliana Raszewski\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, March 15 (Reuters) - Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to license market makers to help stabilize its embattled peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Treasury starts newly announced dollar sales in April, two people with direct knowledge of the plans told Reuters on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The bank hopes the market makers, dealers who agree to buy and sell at set prices, would bolster liquidity in the exchange market to help avoid the sharp gyrations the peso has suffered in recent weeks when it hit a record low of 42.5 pesos per dollar in thin trading.\par \par \uc2 "We are going to take advantage of the existence of this market auction to promote the creation of market makers in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, something that does not exist now," said one of the people. "It is something that we are talking with banks and it will most likely start together with the Treasury bids."\par \par \uc2 Both sources asked not to be named because the plan has not been made public. Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's treasury minister \uc2 Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Dujovne\uc2  revealed on Thursday that the treasury would sell $9.6 billion in dollars from April until the end of the year via daily auctions of $60 million, aiming to acquire pesos to pay for ongoing expenses.\par \par \uc2 The announcement came after a sharp fall in the peso , dragged down by emerging doubts about the progress of the economy and rising political uncertainty generated by the upcoming general elections in October.\par \par \uc2 The second person said the dollar auctions "would provide liquidity at a time when it is possible that, given the uncertainty of the electoral process, the market will have this kind of dynamic," referring to market volatility.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso has remained recently within a non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band that came into effect last year, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned about volatility in a market where there can be low liquidity.\par \par \uc2 "One thing is the value (of the peso), and another thing is when the variations are very abrupt and with little liquidity," the second person said. "That type of dynamic is disruptive." (Reporting by Eliana Raszewski; Editing by Adam Jourdan and Phil Berlowitz) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-3-15T18:48:32.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190315ef3f03b4x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
