\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Argentina \highlight\uc2  adjusts  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  guidelines to combat inflation\b0\par\par\uc2 171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2019\par 00:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Feb 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it had changed its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  guidelines to allow it more flexibility in combating the high inflation blighting the country.\par \par \uc2 The bank raised to $150 million from $75 million the limit of daily sales that can be made after the dollar exceeds the upper limit of its stipulated price band.\par \par \uc2 When the dollar falls below the lower limit of the band, which is modified regularly, the bids may not exceed $50 million per day, from the previous maximum of $75 million.\par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at 39.18 pesos on Thursday, when the bank's non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band was between 38.617 and 49.975 pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 An abrupt depreciation of the peso last year has sparked a financial crisis in Argentina, exacerbated by a prolonged recession and high inflation. (Reporting by Nicolas Misculin; writing by Aislinn Laing; Editing by Rosalba O'Brien) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-3-1T00:21:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190228ef2s03a4t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
