\par\par \b \uc2 Argentine cenbank buys a total of $75 mln in two  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2019\par 16:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Feb 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it bought a total of $75 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, as part of its program of containing the value of the local peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank announced its purchase of $50 million late in the morning at an average price of 37.432 pesos per U.S. dollar. It later said it bought $25 million at an average 37.376 pesos to the greenback. The bank has set a no-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band of 38.021 and 49.203 pesos to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 So far this year the bank has purchased $835 million in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at keeping the peso in the trading band, which was established as part of the country's $56 billion standby financing deal with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Walter Bianchi, writing by Hugh Bronstein Editing by Chizu Nomiyama) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-2-6T16:39:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190206ef2602sdx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
