\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina and its new monetary dilemma: the peso is stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 , president of the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , faces an unusual problem. The peso has recovered so much in recent months that it is conducting tests with a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange designed to help the bank rebuild its credibility.\par \par \uc2 The band was created in September with the endorsement of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , when the peso was losing half of its value in the midst of a massive sale. It was supposed to allow a slow and controlled weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which now floats within a certain range that adjusts daily. If it deviates above or below this range, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can - but is not obligated to - sell or buy dollars to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Few economists expected the peso to become one of the best-performing emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has rebounded 10% against the dollar since the implementation of the plan - which also meant freezing the amount of pesos in circulation and keeping interest rates close to 60 percent - a high global figure. While a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  helps Argentina fight inflation and adjust its external accounts, it could hurt the credibility of the bank again depending on the management of Sandleris.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must communicate its strategy clearly, otherwise its credibility could be compromised," said Priscila Robledo, economist at Continuum Economics.\par \par \uc2 "Buying dollars to increase the liquidity of the peso and at the same time pay extremely high rates to reduce the monetary base does not seem to be the best strategy."\par \par \uc2 Reduction of fees? So far, Sandleris' efforts to defend the band have not worked. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought US $ 190 million since January 10, but the peso has remained mainly below the defined range. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 37.5 per US dollar on Wednesday, within the range of the band.\par \par \uc2 The faster reduction in interest rates could boost debt and economic growth, and at the same time reduce the demand for pesos in the market. But that strategy carries its own risks. The ex-president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Federico Sturzenegger\uc2 , lowered the interest rates in January 2018, only to have to raise them sharply in April. He resigned in June, admitting that he had lost credibility.\par \par \uc2 "What they do not want is to lower rates at a time when confidence has been restored only to raise them again if the dollar rises again," said Sebasti\u225\'00\'E1n Mart\u237\'00\'EDnez, a macroeconomic analyst at Argentine consultancy ABECEB.\par \par \uc2 Much of the recent gains in the peso are simply a correction to last year's losses, combined with an increase in global investors' appetite for risk this year. At a national level, inflation is slowing down and the president, \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 , a favorite of the market, has seen an increase in approval rates.\par \par \uc2 However, there are good reasons to expect that the weight will weaken. Argentina is in the middle of a recession, inflation is expected to close this year around 30% and the uncertainty of the October presidential elections could trigger another \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.\par \par \uc2 "They are going with care but I think they are going to continue buying," said Soledad Tortarolo, head of fixed income research at the Allaria Ledesma & CIA brokerage in Buenos Aires. She predicts that the bank will increase the daily amount it can buy to US $ 150 million. "It is important that they defend the zone of non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  entry and its new monetary dilemma: the peso is stronger was first published in La Tercera.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190117ef1h0083q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw77\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1155\pichgoal600
