\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Argentina peso's slide may test band under \uc2 IMF\uc2  deal- economists\b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2018\par 21:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2018 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with comments from analysts, peso close)\par \par \uc2 By Gabriel Burin and Scott Squires\par \par \uc2 BUENOS AIRES, Sept 28 (Reuters) - Argentina's peso in the coming days could test the limits of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band aimed at stemming \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  under a revised $57 billion agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 , economists said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 As part of the revised deal, Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would establish a trading band for the peso between 34 and 44 per dollar. The band would depreciate daily at a rate that would come to 3 percent per month. As long as the peso stays in the band, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been at the center of emerging market turmoil this year. It lost a further 3.87 percent on Friday to close at 41.3 per dollar, bringing losses for September to 10 percent, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The peso is down nearly 55 percent against the dollar this year as foreign investors fled amid fears President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2 's center-right government might be unable to service its debt next year.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the market looked ready to test the limits of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band next week. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent $16 billion so far this year propping up the peso.\par \par \uc2 "We are concerned that a wide band could lead markets to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and push it to the upper limit of the no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone, even if the peso has already undergone a significant devaluation," \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  said in a report.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also has hiked interest rates to a punishing 60 percent in a failed bid to control inflation, which is expected to top 40 percent by year end.\par \par \uc2 Argentina's new \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  - an economist and academic appointed on Tuesday after his predecessor unexpectedly resigned, said attacking inflation rather than controlling the exchange rate would be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's priority.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures exerted pressure on the peso and the outlook still looks uncertain next week," said Gustavo Quintana, a trader at local brokerage PR Corredores de Cambio.\par \par \uc2 Sandleris met with banking executives on Thursday to discuss raising reserve requirements but there is no date set for any announcement, newspapers Cronista and BAE reported, citing sources present in the meetings. His predecessor \uc2 Luis Caputo\uc2 , a former Wall Street trader, raised reserve requirements several times since July to reduce liquidity.\par \par \uc2 Under the \uc2 IMF\uc2  deal, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped an inflation target in favor of limiting money supply. Sandleris said it will target zero growth in the monetary base until June 2019, down from the current growth rate of 2 percent a month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also discussing a reduction in the amount of short-term debt, known as Lebac, allowed to replace hard cash in bank reserves, the reports said.\par \par \uc2 IMF Managing Director \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  said the financing agreement, the largest in the Fund's history, would boost loan disbursements by $19 billion through the end of 2019 to calm investor fears. (Reporting by Gabriel Burin, Walter Bianchi and Scott Squires Writing by Scott Squires Editing by Daniel Flynn, Steve Orlofsky and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2018-9-28T20:53:05.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020180928ee9s03osm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
