\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Argentina and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  agreed to raise the financial agreement to US $ 57,100 million\b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Argentina reached on Wednesday a new credit agreement with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  ( \uc2 IMF\uc2  ), which raises the stand-by loan of US $ 50,000 million agreed last June to US $ 57,100 million. The multilateral body foresees an acceleration of disbursements, in order to reduce the fiscal deficit to zero next year. Economy Minister \uc2 Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Dujovne\uc2  said the agreement would lead Argentina's GDP to expand 5.2% in 2019.\par \par \uc2 As part of the agreement will proceed with the acceleration of disbursements. The Economy Minister explained that this year the country will receive US $ 13,400 million of the US $ 6,000 originally planned, while in 2019 the amount will rise from US $ 11,400 million to US $ 22,800 million. "These funds are no longer precautionary, but may be used as a budget support," he said.\par \par \uc2 Although the money will not necessarily be used to repay the debt, according to The Guardian as part of the agreement, it was agreed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the peso depreciates below 44 pesos per dollar. It is currently at 39 pesos per dollar after losing 50% of its value since the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 The announcement of the US $ 57.1 billion loan - the largest in the history of the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , according to the agency's director, \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  - comes a day after \uc2 Luis Caputo\uc2 's resignation as president of the Argentine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Caputo, according to Reuters, was an investment banker who had had differences with Dujovne and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  for his handling of the exchange policy. In his place was appointed Guido Sandleris, an academic close to the Minister of Economy.\par \par \uc2 It should be recalled that the \uc2 IMF\uc2  and Argentina signed four financial assistance agreements between 1991 and 2001 and, during that period, the external debt of the southern country went from about US $ 70,000 million at the end of 1990 to more than US $ 140,000 million registered in 2001, according to the newspaper El Pa\u237\'00\'EDs. A 2004 report by the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's internal audit unit concluded that the multilateral body did not provide sufficient oversight and overestimated the growth and success of the economic reforms in 2001.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180927ee9r003tj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
