\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Now bet that the dollar does not exceed 47 pesos at the end of the year\b0\par\par\uc2 1,084 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The government and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  modified the exchange regime. There will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as long as it fluctuates between $ 34 and $ 44. The amounts will rise 3% per month. If the dollar goes up, they will only sell $ 150 million a day.\par \par \uc2 Buenos Aires. The Government and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  agreed to modify the exchange regime of \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2  and from today the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when the price of the dollar pierces a minimum of 34 pesos or exceeds a maximum of 44 pesos, with a monthly adjustment of three hundred.\par \par \uc2 With this new scheme, the administration of \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  is betting that the value of the ticket in the market does not exceed 47 pesos at the end of the year. A level very far from the average price of 40.10 pesos that the Government itself reflected in the 2019 Budget.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2 : US $ 7,100 million more and change in monetary policy The market will give its verdict today after the announcement Caution about politics, with warnings from economists The new regime was explained yesterday by the new president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Guido Sandleris, who replaced the resignation \uc2 Luis Caputo\uc2  and personally negotiated this new scheme with the \uc2 IMF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The official clarified that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will no longer attempt to fix the price of the ticket, as long as it does not leave the established bands.\par \par \uc2 "Argentina is vulnerable to disruptive volatility, since the exchange rate plays a key role in inflation expectations," he said.\par \par \uc2 He added: "These bands should be interpreted as guides on what can be expected from the behavior of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in each zone".\par \par \uc2 From now on, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  observes that there is excessive volatility, that is to say, rises or falls very strong in short periods of time, it will start to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying or selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 The entity will act then when the dollar is below 34 pesos (which is unlikely to happen) or above 44 pesos. If the dollar is located between those points, there will be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 : it is what is called flotation.\par \par \uc2 Maximum expected values\par \par \uc2 Those tips are not fixed. This "band" of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be adjusted daily at a rate of three percent per month until the end of the year. That means that, at the end of October, the ceiling of the dollar will be 44 pesos; in November, of 45.32 pesos, and at the end of December, of 46.68 pesos.\par \par \uc2 If the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exceeds the predicted ceilings, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will go out to the market to sell up to 150 million dollars. With this, it will provide liquidity and will lower -according to Sandleris- the value up to the level intended.\par \par \uc2 The sum that it can offer is not significant in light of what the Central's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were during the run against the peso that began last April.\par \par \uc2 When you sell dollars, the Central will withdraw the pesos and not reinject them in any other way, so that in that way you will reduce more the peso \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower the demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2 "We are aware of the risks that an excessive appreciation of the exchange rate represents for the real economy," said Sandleris.\par \par \uc2 This ensures that the Central will not drop the price of the ticket below what the Government intended, ie 34 pesos.\par \par \uc2 The Cambiemos coalition does not want the economy to lose competitiveness after paying the political cost of the 50 percent devaluation so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Comfortable in 40\par \par \uc2 Sandleris said it yesterday very clearly: "As a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we are very comfortable with the level of the exchange rate that is currently registered."\par \par \uc2 The authorities consider that a rapid nominal appreciation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "a sign of greater confidence", and thatthe demand for pesos will increase. If that happens, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy dollars to swell its reserves.\par \par \uc2 Sandleris believes that the dollar's price bands provide "a very clear and transparent framework" for exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the excessive volatility of the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 That is, it gives predictability to economic agents: investors, savers and consumers.\par \par \uc2 Neither goals nor rates\par \par \uc2 For the head of the BCRA, this "financial storm" showed two vulnerabilities in Argentina: the fiscal deficit and inflation. "As a government, we have made mistakes, underestimated the difficulty of correcting the imbalance received and the speed at which international conditions would change."\par \par \uc2 In this context, Sandleris argued that the "inflation targeting regime did not give the expected results", which is why it will be "left aside", while the agency will now address "the control of the amount of money in the economy". " "We will take the necessary measures so that the monetary base grows zero percent in nominal terms from here to June 2019," he said.\par \par \uc2 The other major change announced yesterday points to interest rates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will no longer fix the reference rate, which is why the 60 percent rate left by \uc2 Luis Caputo\uc2  disappears.\par \par \uc2 As announced yesterday, the reference interest rate of the Leliq will fluctuate daily according to market demand.\par \par \uc2 The core of the agreement point by point\par \par \uc2 The new program with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  that will mark the economy.\par \par \uc2 Insured commitments. The agreement with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  guarantees not to fall into default at least until 2020.\par \par \uc2 More money The credit increased by 7,100 million dollars, so it will be 57,000 million.\par \par \uc2 Disbursements There will be an advance payment of disbursements for this year and 2019. In the remainder of the year will reach 13,400 million and the next will arrive 22,800 million.\par \par \uc2 Back. Macri will have 36,200 million dollars from the \uc2 IMF\uc2  until the end of his term, that is, some 18,800 million more than originally agreed (in June).\par \par \uc2 Available Program funds will no longer be treated as "precautionary" and will be available for use as budget support. That is, the Government may spend the tickets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For the dollar, there will be free float between 34 and 44 pesos initially. If the dollar pierces or exceeds these limits, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy or sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Without inflation goals. The inflation targeting regime was eliminated.\par \par \uc2 Issue. There will be a very strict control over the amount of money in the economy. The monetary base will grow 0% until June 2019.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180927ee9r00112\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
