\par\par \b \uc2 Trump Comments Suggest Nafta Talks With Canada Now on Hold -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,475 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2018\par 00:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 18:59 EDT -- President Trump's remarks about Canada during a press conference on Wednesday suggest Nafta talks between the two countries are now on hold, Toronto trade lawyer \uc2 Lawrence Herman\uc2  says. Trump told reporters he is unhappy with Canada's handling of trade negotiations and threatened to put tariffs on Canadian auto imports if Canada doesn't bend on U.S. dairy demands. "This kind of behavior on the part of a U.S. president, threatening direct economic harm [on Canada] is unprecedented," said Herman, who is also a former Canadian diplomat. He said Trump's comments suggest he "doesn't want to deal with Canada on this issue, at least in the foreseeable future." (Kim.mackrael@wsj.com, @kimmackrael)\par \par \uc2 1855 ET [Dow Jones \}--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it will stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the exchange rate is between 34 pesos to 44 pesos to the US dollar. But if it breaches the upper limit of the so-called "non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  says the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell up to $150M to shore up the peso, which has depreciated sharply this year. The change in policy comes as the \uc2 IMF\uc2  agreed to increase its bailout program for \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after objecting to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  while calling for a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1845 ET - Argentine analysts say the market's reaction to a new deal with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  to boost a bailout package will be important to determine the political impact for President \uc2 Mauricio Macri\uc2  . He is facing social unrest over high inflation and a contracting economy that risks hurting his likely re-election bid late next year. The \uc2 IMF\uc2  agreed today to increase its bailout package by almost 15% to $57.1B, while Argentina says it will tackle inflation by containing the supply of money and halting \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate market. "It is a new experiment, we've never implemented this kind of policy before," says analyst Sergio Bernesztein. Will it help Macri politically? "It depends on how the market is going to react and the impact on the real economy." (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1830 ET [Dow Jones ] -- Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 , says it could take a few months for inflation to start declining after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped inflation targets in favor of monetary base goals to contain the supply of money. "We are attacking the root cause of inflation," Sandleris says. "The objective is that it will decline as fast as possible." The change in policy comes as the \uc2 IMF\uc2  boosted its bailout package for Argentina to $57.1B from $50B. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also committed to not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market when the exchange rate is between 34 pesos to 44 pesos to the USD, Sandleris says. \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a cause of conflict with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  , which supports a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)Amid the \uc2 National Transportation Safety Board\uc2  's investigation of an Air Canada jet that almost crashed on top of airliners on a San Francisco taxiway last year, vice chairman \uc2 Bruce Landsberg\uc2  tried to take the heat off portions of the aviation industry. In a move seemingly reflecting the Trump Administration's broad deregulatory bent, he proposed to exclude certain private and business aircraft from board recommendations to implement enhanced cockpit alerting systems for mistaken landing approaches. But the revised language eventually was withdrawn, after board chairman \uc2 Robert Sumwalt\uc2  pointedly countered by emphasizing the board's traditional approach of refraining from cost assessments: "I do not believe this agency should be concerned," the chairman said, about championing safety changes "with a burden on the industry." andy.pasztor@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 1741 ET - \uc2 Sonic Automotive\uc2  Chief Executive Scott Smith has stepped down after leading one of the nation's largest dealership chains for more than 20 years. He will remain with the company in his role as co-founder. \uc2 David Smith\uc2 , who has most recently been the company's executive vice chairman, was named CEO. \uc2 Jeff Dyke\uc2  is now the president of Sonic after serving as the company's executive vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2008. The announcement comes almost exactly a week after \uc2 AutoNation\uc2  longtime Chief Executive \uc2 Mike Jackson\uc2  announced he would step down next year. \uc2 AutoNation\uc2  's board is conducting a search for a new CEO. (adrienne.roberts@wsj.com; @AdrRoberts)\par \par \uc2 1707 ET - \uc2 Amazon\uc2  says it's opening a new store: This time in New York, with top sellers from its website. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  4-star is located in SoHo and will feature small kitchen appliances, tech gadgets and books, among other items. It adds to \uc2 Amazon\uc2  's existing book stores, cashier- less Go stores, device pop-up stores and, of course, \uc2 Whole Foods\uc2  . \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has been working to reinvent the physical shopping experience, and the 4-star store is the latest attempt. (laura.stevens@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1649 ET - The peso firmed against the US dollar after the Fed raised interest rates as expected and reiterated its likely interest-rate path. The peso was quoted in Mexico City at 18.8580 to the dollar compared with 19.00 Tuesday, and local government debt rallied, pushing yields down. Banorte said Fed action could put pressure on the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  , which it expects will raise interest rates at next week's meeting. "In general the outlook of tighter US monetary conditions is a significant challenge for emerging markets, which could partially contaminate Mexican assets despite strong fundamentals," Banorte said. The IPC stock index slipped 0.1% to 49,606 points. (anthony.harrup@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1641 ET - The \uc2 Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  sues \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  for age discrimination, saying the railroad operator denied jobs to qualified applicants over the age of 52. The agency alleges that the company preferred to hire people under 52 for special agent jobs, part of the firm's law enforcement and security \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because managers assumed older workers would retire soon after joining the company. The \uc2 EEOC\uc2  says \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  's actions violate the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, which prohibits discrimination against workers over age 40. The lawsuit seeks lost wages and changes to the company's employment practices. "The company is confident that an unbiased assessment of the facts will demonstrate the fairness and integrity involved in its employment processes," \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  said in a statement. (lauren.weber@wsj.com; @laurenweberWSJ)\par \par \uc2 1633 ET - Saudi Arabia puts the US on a short list of countries it will negotiate with to build nuclear power plants in the kingdom, Energy Secretary Rick Perry says. Saudi Arabia is looking to build its first of what could be several reactors, potentially creating a new market worth tens of billions of dollars that has drawn interest from Russia, South Korea and China among others. In an on-the-record session with reporters Perry didn't name the other countries that made the list and tried to walk back his comments after his staff told him the decision wasn't yet public. "The negotiations continue to go forward," Perry says, before retreating. (tim.puko@wsj.com; @timpuko)\par \par \uc2 1618 ET - Shares of financial companies in the S&P 500 tumbled into the close, logging their biggest one-day loss since July. The S&P 500 financial sector ended the day down 1.3%, with heavyweight \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  losing 1.6% and \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  shedding 1.8%. Partly to blame for the sector's selloff: a rally in Treasurys, which picked up steam after Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  concluded his press conference with some cautionary comments about stock valuations. The yield on the 10-year Treasury yield, which had been trading closer to 3.080% before the Fed released its policy statement, was recently at 3.050% and around its low for the day. (akane.otani@wsj.com; @akaneotani)\par \par \uc2 1610 ET - The \uc2 Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  sues \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  for age discrimination, saying the railroad operator denied jobs to qualified applicants over the age of 52. The agency alleges that the company preferred to hire people under 52 for special agent jobs, part of the firm's law enforcement and security \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because managers assumed older workers would retire soon after joining the company. The \uc2 EEOC\uc2  says \uc2 Norfolk Southern\uc2  's actions violate the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, which prohibits discrimination against workers over age 40. The lawsuit seeks lost wages and changes to the company's employment practices. The company did not immediately respond to a request for comment. (lauren.weber@wsj.com; @laurenweberWSJ)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 26, 2018 18:59 ET (22:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180926ee9q003e4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
