\par\par \b \uc2 Global Energy Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2018\par 01:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering Energy markets. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 1917 ET -- \uc2 Santos\uc2 's ambitions of driving annual production to 100 million barrels by 2025 appears achievable and should help with a leg-up in the share price should crude prices remain near current levels, \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  suggests. The investment bank expects the market will focus for now on the energy company's debt profile, given the strong underlying themes for the industry. It remains bullish on the shares, and lifts its target 19%, to A$8.30. Down 1.1% yesterday, to A$7.25, shares have jumped 33% so far in 2018. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; @RobbMStewart)18:59 EDT -- President Trump's remarks about Canada during a press conference on Wednesday suggest Nafta talks between the two countries are now on hold, Toronto trade lawyer \uc2 Lawrence Herman\uc2  says. Trump told reporters he is unhappy with Canada's handling of trade negotiations and threatened to put tariffs on Canadian auto imports if Canada doesn't bend on U.S. dairy demands. "This kind of behavior on the part of a U.S. president, threatening direct economic harm [on Canada] is unprecedented," said Herman, who is also a former Canadian diplomat. He said Trump's comments suggest he "doesn't want to deal with Canada on this issue, at least in the foreseeable future." (Kim.mackrael@wsj.com, @kimmackrael)\par \par \uc2 1855 ET [Dow Jones \}--\b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it will stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when the exchange rate is between 34 pesos to 44 pesos to the US dollar. But if it breaches the upper limit of the so-called "non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  zone," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2  says the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sell up to $150M to shore up the peso, which has depreciated sharply this year. The change in policy comes as the \uc2 IMF\uc2  agreed to increase its bailout program for \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after objecting to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  while calling for a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1830 ET [Dow Jones ] -- Argentina's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president, \uc2 Guido Sandleris\uc2 , says it could take a few months for inflation to start declining after the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped inflation targets in favor of monetary base goals to contain the supply of money. "We are attacking the root cause of inflation," Sandleris says. "The objective is that it will decline as fast as possible." The change in policy comes as the \uc2 IMF\uc2  boosted its bailout package for Argentina to $57.1B from $50B. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also committed to not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market when the exchange rate is between 34 pesos to 44 pesos to the USD, Sandleris says. \b \highlight22\uc2 Argentina\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a cause of conflict with the \uc2 IMF\uc2  , which supports a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1633 ET - Saudi Arabia puts the US on a short list of countries it will negotiate with to build nuclear power plants in the kingdom, Energy Secretary Rick Perry says. Saudi Arabia is looking to build its first of what could be several reactors, potentially creating a new market worth tens of billions of dollars that has drawn interest from Russia, South Korea and China among others. In an on-the-record session with reporters Perry didn't name the other countries that made the list and tried to walk back his comments after his staff told him the decision wasn't yet public. "The negotiations continue to go forward," Perry says, before retreating. (tim.puko@wsj.com; @timpuko)\par \par \uc2 1232 ET - The Bel-20 closes 0.2% lower at 3743.58 amid mixed trading in global markets ahead of the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  's rate decision later in the day. Belgium's local and international postal-services company \uc2 bpost SA\uc2  was the worst performer with a 2.6% decline, trailed by a 2.1% drop in the shares of \uc2 Telenet Group Holding NV\uc2  , Belgium's largest provider of cable broadband services. Among the companies that bucked the downturn: French energy firm \uc2 Engie SA\uc2  with a 1.3% rise making it the benchmark's best performer. (emre.peker@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1208 ET - Instinet sees the higher costs for feedstocks like ethane, used to make plastics, cutting into \uc2 DowDuPont\uc2  's margins and keeping pressure on near-term earnings. The investment bank drops the chemical giant to neutral and lowers price target to $76 from $81, expecting shares to remain rangebound over the next few months. \uc2 Instinet\uc2  says it still views \uc2 DowDuPont\uc2  as an "attractive core holding in large cap chemicals," but more "patience" will be required on the part of investors. \uc2 DowDuPont\uc2  shares off 1.3% to $67.06. (patrick.sheridan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1146 ET - Oil investors wondering if the typically low-demand fall season was ever going to arrive got their answer Wednesday, as the EIA's weekly report revealed a huge drop in refinery activity, rising oil inventories and a large drop in demand. The EIA said oil stockpiles climbed 1.9M bbls vs consensus for a 1.3M-bbl decline, while refinery activity plunged 5 percentage points to 90.4% vs expectations for just a 0.9 percentage point decline. And motor gasoline supplied to the market, a proxy for demand, plunged to 9M bpd vs 9.5M a week earlier. "Demand is weak, and it's getting weaker," Stephen Schork of The Schork Report tells WSJ. The \uc2 Nymex\uc2  oil contract for November moves 0.7% lower to $71.80/bbl. (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1134 ET - Europe's steel market isn't likely to cool down in 2019, though the "huge growth" of the past year should begin to subside, \uc2 Tata Steel Europe\uc2  's Chief Commercial Officer \uc2 Henrik Adam\uc2  says. Demand for steel remains undented in Europe--despite uncertainty surrounding trade disputes--but steelmakers will have to contend with higher prices for inputs, particularly energy, zinc and tin, Mr. Adam says. Uncertainty over raw material prices will be a key factor in negotiating steel prices in 2019, he says. "Anyone hoping for price reductions against this background is hoping in vain." (nathan.allen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0808 ET - Oil prices decline after three straight sessions of increases following a weekly report that points to rising US inventories of crude oil. Industry group API said Tuesday US crude oil stockpiles rose 2.9M bbls last week, and that gasoline inventories rose nearly 1M bbls. That suggests today's official EIA report, due at 10:30am ET, may also show bearish increases, despite a WSJ survey of analysts forecasting a 1.3M-bbl crude decline, and just a 200k-bbl rise in gasoline supplies. Brent, the global benchmark, falls 0.5% to $80.85/bbl after hitting a four-year high Tuesday, while the US benchmark WTI declines 0.6% to $71.86 after closing at an 11-week high Tuesday. (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0747 ET - \uc2 Glencore\uc2  is likely to keep its credit edge over rival \uc2 Anglo American\uc2  into next year, says \uc2 Moody's\uc2  . The credit-rating agency notes that the credit quality of both companies has recovered since the commodity downturn ended in 2016. "But \uc2 Glencore\uc2  's credit quality will remain stronger into 2019 thanks to its more robust business profile and better resilience to a future downturn - provided that the the \uc2 U.S. Department of Justice\uc2  's recent demand for information doesn't lead to any large fines for the company or a reassessment of its business risk," says Sven Reinke, Senior Vice President at \uc2 Moody's\uc2 . (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0719 ET - Shares in miners fall after the price of copper drops as Chinese traders dump preholiday supply. \uc2 BHP Billiton\uc2  shares retreat nearly 1% and Chilean copper miner Antofagasta backtracks 0.7%. "\uc2 London Metal Exchange\uc2  copper falls for the third day, extending the drop from a two-month high at the close of last week, as Chinese traders release supply ahead of the week-long Golden Week national holiday despite signs of rising demand from Chile," analysts at mining specialist brokerage S.P. Angel say. They note that copper closed 4.6% higher at $6,363 a ton on Friday, the highest since July 9. At 1209 BST the price was down 0.7% at $6,272 a ton. (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 26, 2018 19:17 ET (23:17 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180926ee9q003k4\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or op